window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b052-8643f91767c1e90b.json"]={sha256:"8643f91767c1e90b3884ccd6592c10e7a5fb84c6ea9b96d3f42d8ff2e30ad2e9",value:{"id":"b052","title":"懸索橋主纜除濕系統","titleEn":"Suspension-cable dehumidification systems","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"主纜內部的水分會先消耗鍍鋅層、再腐蝕高強度鋼絲，而主纜幾乎無法更換。本課以本州四國連絡橋首創的主纜乾燥空氣送氣（管理目標相對濕度 40%）與大貝爾特東橋 2014 至 2015 年的除濕改造為主軸，說明腐蝕門檻與露點、送氣與排氣流路、彈性體包覆與索夾密封、除濕機與預冷、改造施工與啟動乾燥曲線、感測器判讀與開纜比對，最後以能耗與生命週期比較說明業主如何決策。","summaryEn":"Moisture inside a main cable first consumes the zinc and then corrodes high-strength wire, and the cable can almost never be replaced. Built around the Honshu-Shikoku bridges' pioneering dry-air cable injection (managed to 40% relative humidity) and the 2014–2015 dehumidification retrofit of the Great Belt East Bridge, this course explains corrosion thresholds and dew point, injection and exhaust flow paths, elastomeric wrapping and cable-band seals, dehumidifiers and pre-coolers, retrofit construction and the start-up dry-out curve, sensor interpretation and comparison with cable openings, and finally energy use and the life-cycle comparison behind an owner's decision.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-suspension","subcategoryTitle":"懸索橋巨作與主纜系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Suspension bridges and main-cable systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-suspension","learningTags":["structures","st-suspension","cable"],"architectureFamily":"cable","architectureNodes":[["除濕機組與預冷","Dehumidifiers and pre-coolers"],["送氣管與送氣套筒","Supply ducts and injection sleeves"],["主纜空隙流路","Flow path through cable voids"],["彈性體包覆與索夾密封","Elastomeric wrap and band seals"],["排氣套筒與感測器","Exhaust sleeves and sensors"],["監控平台與開纜檢查","Monitoring platform and cable openings"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[3,2],[2,4],[4,5],[5,0]],"diagram":{"type":"cable","labels":["除濕機組與預冷","送氣管與送氣套筒","主纜空隙流路","彈性體包覆與索夾密封","排氣套筒與感測器"],"labelsEn":["Dehumidifiers and pre-coolers","Supply ducts and injection sleeves","Flow path through cable voids","Elastomeric wrap and band seals","Exhaust sleeves and sensors"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：為一段 300 m 的主纜區段規劃送氣。主纜直徑 0.87 m、空隙率 20%，空隙體積約 0.594×0.20×300 ≈ 35.7 m³。若在中央送氣、兩端排氣，每側流動距離 150 m；以等效滲透率 1×10⁻⁹ m²、流動斷面 0.6 m²、壓差 2,000 Pa 估算，每側流量約 27 L/min，合計約 53 L/min（3.2 m³/h），每天換氣約 76.8 m³，約為空隙體積的 2.2 倍。送入 25 °C、15% RH 空氣（約 3.4 g/m³），出口 40% RH（約 9.2 g/m³），每天可帶走約 0.44 kg 水。若段內殘留 10 kg 水，約需 23 天；若改為只在一端送氣、另一端排氣，流動距離 300 m 使流量減為約 13 L/min，乾燥時間增為約 91 天。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際橋梁的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: plan injection for a 300 m cable section. The cable is 0.87 m in diameter with 20% voids, a void volume of about 0.594×0.20×300 ≈ 35.7 m³. Injecting at mid-length with exhausts at both ends gives a 150 m flow length each way; with equivalent permeability 1×10⁻⁹ m², flow section 0.6 m² and 2,000 Pa, each side carries about 27 L/min, about 53 L/min (3.2 m³/h) in total, or about 76.8 m³ a day, about 2.2 times the void volume. Injecting air at 25 °C and 15% RH (about 3.4 g/m³) with exhaust at 40% RH (about 9.2 g/m³) removes about 0.44 kg of water a day, so 10 kg of trapped water takes about 23 days. Injecting at one end and exhausting at the other makes the flow length 300 m, cutting flow to about 13 L/min and stretching drying to about 91 days. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b052-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「主纜為何從內部腐蝕」與「系統構成與送氣間距」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Why cables corrode from the inside\" and \"System layout and injection spacing\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b052-v13-01","title":"主纜為何從內部腐蝕：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Why cables corrode from the inside: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「主纜內部露點」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dew point inside the cable” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲平行排列，鋼絲之間約有兩成空隙。水分在紡線或牽引期間隨雨水進入，也會從纏絲裂縫、索夾邊緣與吊索附近滲入，並在主纜低點聚積。白天日照加熱、夜間輻射冷卻，主纜內部空氣反覆「呼吸」，帶入潮濕空氣；當鋼絲表面溫度低於空氣露點，水氣就凝結在鋼絲上。本州四國連絡橋拆開舊橋纏絲時發現鋼絲已經生鏽，大貝爾特東橋的業主也參考了福斯公路橋的腐蝕教訓，這些經驗說明外部塗裝無法保證內部乾燥。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主纜內部露點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A main cable holds tens of thousands of parallel wires with about one-fifth of its section as voids. Water enters with rain during spinning or hauling and later seeps in through cracked wrapping, cable-band edges and around hangers, collecting at low points. Daytime sun heats the cable and night-time radiation cools it, so the air inside breathes in and out, drawing in humid air; when the wire surface falls below the air's dew point, vapour condenses on the wires. The Honshu-Shikoku authority found rust on wires when it removed the wrapping of older bridges, and the Great Belt owner drew on corrosion found on the Forth Road Bridge, showing that external paint cannot guarantee a dry interior. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dew point inside the cable” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Magnus 式露點 T_d = b·γ/(a − γ)，γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T)，a = 17.62、b = 243.12 °C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Magnus dew point T_d = b·γ/(a − γ), with γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T), a = 17.62 and b = 243.12 °C.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主纜內部露點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dew point inside the cable”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-01-k1","title":"主纜為何從內部腐蝕","titleEn":"Why cables corrode from the inside","text":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲平行排列，鋼絲之間約有兩成空隙。水分在紡線或牽引期間隨雨水進入，也會從纏絲裂縫、索夾邊緣與吊索附近滲入，並在主纜低點聚積。","textEn":"A main cable holds tens of thousands of parallel wires with about one-fifth of its section as voids. Water enters with rain during spinning or hauling and later seeps in through cracked wrapping, cable-band edges and around hangers, collecting at low points.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜為何從內部腐蝕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Why cables corrode from the inside\" is correct?","options":["主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。","主纜由數萬根鋼絲平行排列，鋼絲之間約有兩成空隙。","只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。"],"optionsEn":["With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside.","A main cable holds tens of thousands of parallel wires with about one-fifth of its section as voids.","Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲平行排列，鋼絲之間約有兩成空隙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A main cable holds tens of thousands of parallel wires with about one-fifth of its section as voids. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b052-v13-02","title":"主纜為何從內部腐蝕：定量估算","titleEn":"Why cables corrode from the inside: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主纜內部露點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dew point inside the cable” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Magnus 式露點 T_d = b·γ/(a − γ)，γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T)，a = 17.62、b = 243.12 °C。纜內空氣 25 °C、80% RH：γ ≈ −0.223 + 1.643 = 1.420，T_d ≈ 21.3 °C，夜間鋼絲只要降到 21 °C 以下就結露；若纜內維持 40% RH，T_d ≈ 10.5 °C，結露機會大幅降低。溫濕度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Magnus dew point T_d = b·γ/(a − γ), with γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T), a = 17.62 and b = 243.12 °C. For cable air at 25 °C and 80% RH: γ ≈ −0.223 + 1.643 = 1.420 and T_d ≈ 21.3 °C, so wires cooling below 21 °C at night collect condensation; held at 40% RH, T_d ≈ 10.5 °C and condensation becomes much rarer. Temperatures and humidities are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在主纜低點與高點各置溫濕度探頭與鋼絲表面溫度計，連續記錄數週，計算每小時露點與鋼絲溫度差，統計結露時數；同時在低點開窗檢查積水與鍍鋅狀態，確認量測推論與實況一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place humidity and temperature probes and wire-surface thermometers at cable low and high points, record continuously for several weeks, compute hourly dew point against wire temperature and count condensation hours; open an inspection window at a low point to check for standing water and zinc condition, confirming that inference matches reality.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Magnus 式露點 T_d = b·γ/(a − γ)，γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T)，a = 17.62、b = 243.12 °C。纜內空氣 25 °C、80% RH：γ ≈ −0.223 + 1.643 = 1.420，T_d ≈ 21.3 °C，夜間鋼絲只要降到 21 °C 以下就結露；若纜內維持 40% RH，T_d ≈ 10.5 °C，結露機會大幅降低。溫濕度為教學假設。","textEn":"Magnus dew point T_d = b·γ/(a − γ), with γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T), a = 17.62 and b = 243.12 °C. For cable air at 25 °C and 80% RH: γ ≈ −0.223 + 1.643 = 1.420 and T_d ≈ 21.3 °C, so wires cooling below 21 °C at night collect condensation; held at 40% RH, T_d ≈ 10.5 °C and condensation becomes much rarer. Temperatures and humidities are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜為何從內部腐蝕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Why cables corrode from the inside\", which statement holds?","options":["除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。","除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","Magnus 式露點 T_d = b·γ/(a − γ)，γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T)，a = 17.62、b = 243.12 °C。"],"optionsEn":["Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do.","Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","Magnus dew point T_d = b·γ/(a − γ), with γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T), a = 17.62 and b = 243.12 °C."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Magnus 式露點 T_d = b·γ/(a − γ)，γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T)，a = 17.62、b = 243.12 °C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Magnus dew point T_d = b·γ/(a − γ), with γ = ln(RH/100) + a·T/(b + T), a = 17.62 and b = 243.12 °C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b052-v13-03","title":"主纜為何從內部腐蝕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Why cables corrode from the inside: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主纜內部露點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dew point inside the cable” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在主纜低點與高點各置溫濕度探頭與鋼絲表面溫度計，連續記錄數週，計算每小時露點與鋼絲溫度差，統計結露時數；同時在低點開窗檢查積水與鍍鋅狀態，確認量測推論與實況一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place humidity and temperature probes and wire-surface thermometers at cable low and high points, record continuously for several weeks, compute hourly dew point against wire temperature and count condensation hours; open an inspection window at a low point to check for standing water and zinc condition, confirming that inference matches reality. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：新建懸索橋應在設計階段就把主纜除濕列為防蝕系統的一部分，並在施工期間限制雨中紡線或牽引、在擠壓前排水；既有橋梁則以溫濕度量測與開窗檢查建立現況基準，再決定是否改造。","observationEn":"Site practice: New suspension bridges should include cable dehumidification in the corrosion-protection design from the start, limiting spinning or hauling in rain and draining before compaction; for existing bridges, establish a baseline by humidity measurement and inspection windows before deciding on a retrofit.","failure":"注意干擾：主纜低點長期積水時，鍍鋅層先被消耗，接著鋼絲出現點蝕與應力腐蝕裂紋；由於外層纏絲完好，問題往往在數十年後開纜檢查才被發現，屆時斷絲與強度損失可能已需要限載或補強。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Where water sits at low points for years, zinc is consumed first and then wires pit and develop stress-corrosion cracks; because the outer wrapping looks intact, the problem is often found only at a cable opening decades later, when broken wires and strength loss may already require load limits or strengthening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在主纜低點與高點各置溫濕度探頭與鋼絲表面溫度計，連續記錄數週，計算每小時露點與鋼絲溫度差，統計結露時數；同時在低點開窗檢查積水與鍍鋅狀態，確認量測推論與實況一致。","textEn":"Place humidity and temperature probes and wire-surface thermometers at cable low and high points, record continuously for several weeks, compute hourly dew point against wire temperature and count condensation hours; open an inspection window at a low point to check for standing water and zinc condition, confirming that inference matches reality.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"新建懸索橋應在設計階段就把主纜除濕列為防蝕系統的一部分，並在施工期間限制雨中紡線或牽引、在擠壓前排水；既有橋梁則以溫濕度量測與開窗檢查建立現況基準，再決定是否改造。","textEn":"New suspension bridges should include cable dehumidification in the corrosion-protection design from the start, limiting spinning or hauling in rain and draining before compaction; for existing bridges, establish a baseline by humidity measurement and inspection windows before deciding on a retrofit.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜為何從內部腐蝕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Why cables corrode from the inside\"?","options":["在主纜低點與高點各置溫濕度探頭與鋼絲表面溫度計，連續記錄數週，計算每小時露點與鋼絲溫度差，統計結露時數。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Place humidity and temperature probes and wire-surface thermometers at cable low and high points, record continuously for several weeks, compute hourly dew point against wire temperature and count condensation hours.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在主纜低點與高點各置溫濕度探頭與鋼絲表面溫度計，連續記錄數週，計算每小時露點與鋼絲溫度差，統計結露時數；同時在低點開窗檢查積水與鍍鋅狀態，確認量測推論與實況一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place humidity and temperature probes and wire-surface thermometers at cable low and high points, record continuously for several weeks, compute hourly dew point against wire temperature and count condensation hours; open an inspection window at a low point to check for standing water and zinc condition, confirming that inference matches reality. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b052-v13-04","title":"主纜為何從內部腐蝕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Why cables corrode from the inside: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主纜內部露點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dew point inside the cable” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"主纜低點長期積水時，鍍鋅層先被消耗，接著鋼絲出現點蝕與應力腐蝕裂紋；由於外層纏絲完好，問題往往在數十年後開纜檢查才被發現，屆時斷絲與強度損失可能已需要限載或補強。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Where water sits at low points for years, zinc is consumed first and then wires pit and develop stress-corrosion cracks; because the outer wrapping looks intact, the problem is often found only at a cable opening decades later, when broken wires and strength loss may already require load limits or strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本州四國連絡橋拆開舊橋纏絲時發現鋼絲已經生鏽，大貝爾特東橋的業主也參考了福斯公路橋的腐蝕教訓，這些經驗說明外部塗裝無法保證內部乾燥。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Honshu-Shikoku authority found rust on wires when it removed the wrapping of older bridges, and the Great Belt owner drew on corrosion found on the Forth Road Bridge, showing that external paint cannot guarantee a dry interior.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"主纜低點長期積水時，鍍鋅層先被消耗，接著鋼絲出現點蝕與應力腐蝕裂紋；由於外層纏絲完好，問題往往在數十年後開纜檢查才被發現，屆時斷絲與強度損失可能已需要限載或補強。","textEn":"Where water sits at low points for years, zinc is consumed first and then wires pit and develop stress-corrosion cracks; because the outer wrapping looks intact, the problem is often found only at a cable opening decades later, when broken wires and strength loss may already require load limits or strengthening.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜為何從內部腐蝕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Why cables corrode from the inside\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","主纜低點長期積水時，鍍鋅層先被消耗，接著鋼絲出現點蝕與應力腐蝕裂紋。","只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Where water sits at low points for years, zinc is consumed first and then wires pit and develop stress-corrosion cracks.","Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜低點長期積水時，鍍鋅層先被消耗，接著鋼絲出現點蝕與應力腐蝕裂紋；由於外層纏絲完好，問題往往在數十年後開纜檢查才被發現，屆時斷絲與強度損失可能已需要限載或補強。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Where water sits at low points for years, zinc is consumed first and then wires pit and develop stress-corrosion cracks; because the outer wrapping looks intact, the problem is often found only at a cable opening decades later, when broken wires and strength loss may already require load limits or strengthening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b052-v13-05","title":"系統構成與送氣間距：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"System layout and injection spacing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「送氣與排氣流路」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Injection and exhaust path” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜除濕系統由除濕機組、風機、送氣管、送氣套筒、氣密包覆、排氣套筒與感測器組成。乾燥空氣從送氣套筒進入主纜，沿鋼絲間的空隙向兩側流動，一路吸收水分，再從一定距離外的排氣套筒排出。主纜空隙像多孔介質，流量與壓差成正比、與流動距離成反比，因此送氣與排氣的間距、送氣壓力與包覆所能承受的壓力，三者必須一起設計。大貝爾特東橋的業主說明，包覆與索夾周圍的密封就是為了讓空氣能在進氣與排氣套筒之間流動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「送氣與排氣流路」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A cable dehumidification system consists of dehumidifier units, fans, supply ducts, injection sleeves, an airtight wrap, exhaust sleeves and sensors. Dry air enters the cable at an injection sleeve, flows both ways through the voids between wires picking up moisture, and leaves at exhaust sleeves some distance away. The cable voids behave like a porous medium, with flow proportional to pressure difference and inversely proportional to flow distance, so sleeve spacing, supply pressure and the pressure the wrap can hold must be designed together. The Great Belt owner explains that the wrapping and the seals around the clamps exist precisely so that air can flow between the inlet and exhaust sleeves. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Injection and exhaust path” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 Darcy 式估算 Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate with Darcy's law Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「送氣與排氣流路」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Injection and exhaust path”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-05-k1","title":"系統構成與送氣間距","titleEn":"System layout and injection spacing","text":"主纜除濕系統由除濕機組、風機、送氣管、送氣套筒、氣密包覆、排氣套筒與感測器組成。乾燥空氣從送氣套筒進入主纜，沿鋼絲間的空隙向兩側流動，一路吸收水分，再從一定距離外的排氣套筒排出。","textEn":"A cable dehumidification system consists of dehumidifier units, fans, supply ducts, injection sleeves, an airtight wrap, exhaust sleeves and sensors. Dry air enters the cable at an injection sleeve, flows both ways through the voids between wires picking up moisture, and leaves at exhaust sleeves some distance away.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「系統構成與送氣間距」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"System layout and injection spacing\" is correct?","options":["只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。","包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。","主纜除濕系統由除濕機組、風機、送氣管、送氣套筒、氣密包覆、排氣套筒與感測器組成。"],"optionsEn":["Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself.","The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.","A cable dehumidification system consists of dehumidifier units, fans, supply ducts, injection sleeves, an airtight wrap, exhaust sleeves and sensors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主纜除濕系統由除濕機組、風機、送氣管、送氣套筒、氣密包覆、排氣套筒與感測器組成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A cable dehumidification system consists of dehumidifier units, fans, supply ducts, injection sleeves, an airtight wrap, exhaust sleeves and sensors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b052-v13-06","title":"系統構成與送氣間距：定量估算","titleEn":"System layout and injection spacing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「送氣與排氣流路」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Injection and exhaust path” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 Darcy 式估算 Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L)。取等效滲透率 k = 1×10⁻⁹ m²、流動斷面 A = 0.6 m²、壓差 Δp = 2,000 Pa、空氣黏滯係數 μ = 1.8×10⁻⁵ Pa·s：流動距離 L = 150 m 時 Q ≈ 4.4×10⁻⁴ m³/s（約 27 L/min）；L 增為 300 m，Q 減半為約 13 L/min。k 與壓差為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate with Darcy's law Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L). With equivalent permeability k = 1×10⁻⁹ m², flow section A = 0.6 m², pressure difference Δp = 2,000 Pa and air viscosity μ = 1.8×10⁻⁵ Pa·s: a flow length L = 150 m gives Q ≈ 4.4×10⁻⁴ m³/s (about 27 L/min); doubling L to 300 m halves Q to about 13 L/min. k and the pressure difference are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表性區段以不同送氣壓力量測進、排氣口流量，反算等效滲透率，確認設計間距下的流量足以在目標時間內乾燥；若不同區段的滲透率差異很大，調整送氣分配或增設套筒。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: On representative sections measure inlet and exhaust flow at several supply pressures, back-calculate equivalent permeability and confirm that flow at the design spacing dries the section in the target time; where permeability varies widely between sections, rebalance supply or add sleeves.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 Darcy 式估算 Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L)。取等效滲透率 k = 1×10⁻⁹ m²、流動斷面 A = 0.6 m²、壓差 Δp = 2,000 Pa、空氣黏滯係數 μ = 1.8×10⁻⁵ Pa·s：流動距離 L = 150 m 時 Q ≈ 4.4×10⁻⁴ m³/s（約 27 L/min）；L 增為 300 m，Q 減半為約 13 L/min。k 與壓差為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate with Darcy's law Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L). With equivalent permeability k = 1×10⁻⁹ m², flow section A = 0.6 m², pressure difference Δp = 2,000 Pa and air viscosity μ = 1.8×10⁻⁵ Pa·s: a flow length L = 150 m gives Q ≈ 4.4×10⁻⁴ m³/s (about 27 L/min); doubling L to 300 m halves Q to about 13 L/min. k and the pressure difference are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「系統構成與送氣間距」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"System layout and injection spacing\", which statement holds?","options":["以 Darcy 式估算 Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L)。","除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。","只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate with Darcy's law Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L).","A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather.","If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 Darcy 式估算 Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate with Darcy's law Q = k·A·Δp/(μ·L). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b052-v13-07","title":"系統構成與送氣間距：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"System layout and injection spacing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「送氣與排氣流路」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Injection and exhaust path” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表性區段以不同送氣壓力量測進、排氣口流量，反算等效滲透率，確認設計間距下的流量足以在目標時間內乾燥；若不同區段的滲透率差異很大，調整送氣分配或增設套筒。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"On representative sections measure inlet and exhaust flow at several supply pressures, back-calculate equivalent permeability and confirm that flow at the design spacing dries the section in the target time; where permeability varies widely between sections, rebalance supply or add sleeves. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：系統設計報告應列出每個區段的長度、預估滲透率、設計壓力與流量、包覆容許壓力與排氣目標，並在試運轉時以實測值更新；任何區段流量偏低都要在交接前處理。","observationEn":"Site practice: The system design report should list each section's length, estimated permeability, design pressure and flow, wrap pressure limit and exhaust target, updated with measured values at commissioning; any section with low flow must be resolved before handover.","failure":"注意干擾：送氣間距過大或壓力不足，遠離送氣口的區段幾乎沒有流量，排氣口讀值卻可能因為近端空氣短路而看似乾燥；壓力過高則超過包覆與索夾密封的承受能力，造成鼓起、剝離與大量洩漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Spacing too long or pressure too low leaves sections far from the inlet with almost no flow, while exhaust readings may still look dry because air short-circuits near the inlet; pressure too high exceeds what the wrap and band seals can hold, causing bulging, debonding and heavy leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表性區段以不同送氣壓力量測進、排氣口流量，反算等效滲透率，確認設計間距下的流量足以在目標時間內乾燥；若不同區段的滲透率差異很大，調整送氣分配或增設套筒。","textEn":"On representative sections measure inlet and exhaust flow at several supply pressures, back-calculate equivalent permeability and confirm that flow at the design spacing dries the section in the target time; where permeability varies widely between sections, rebalance supply or add sleeves.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"系統設計報告應列出每個區段的長度、預估滲透率、設計壓力與流量、包覆容許壓力與排氣目標，並在試運轉時以實測值更新；任何區段流量偏低都要在交接前處理。","textEn":"The system design report should list each section's length, estimated permeability, design pressure and flow, wrap pressure limit and exhaust target, updated with measured values at commissioning; any section with low flow must be resolved before handover.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「系統構成與送氣間距」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"System layout and injection spacing\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在代表性區段以不同送氣壓力量測進、排氣口流量，反算等效滲透率，確認設計間距下的流量足以在目標時間內乾燥；若不同區段的滲透率差異很大，調整送氣分配或增設套筒。","除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","On representative sections measure inlet and exhaust flow at several supply pressures, back-calculate equivalent permeability and confirm that flow at the design spacing dries the section in the target time.","Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在代表性區段以不同送氣壓力量測進、排氣口流量，反算等效滲透率，確認設計間距下的流量足以在目標時間內乾燥；若不同區段的滲透率差異很大，調整送氣分配或增設套筒。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"On representative sections measure inlet and exhaust flow at several supply pressures, back-calculate equivalent permeability and confirm that flow at the design spacing dries the section in the target time; where permeability varies widely between sections, rebalance supply or add sleeves. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b052-v13-08","title":"系統構成與送氣間距：失效診斷","titleEn":"System layout and injection spacing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「送氣與排氣流路」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Injection and exhaust path” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"送氣間距過大或壓力不足，遠離送氣口的區段幾乎沒有流量，排氣口讀值卻可能因為近端空氣短路而看似乾燥；壓力過高則超過包覆與索夾密封的承受能力，造成鼓起、剝離與大量洩漏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Spacing too long or pressure too low leaves sections far from the inlet with almost no flow, while exhaust readings may still look dry because air short-circuits near the inlet; pressure too high exceeds what the wrap and band seals can hold, causing bulging, debonding and heavy leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：大貝爾特東橋的業主說明，包覆與索夾周圍的密封就是為了讓空氣能在進氣與排氣套筒之間流動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Great Belt owner explains that the wrapping and the seals around the clamps exist precisely so that air can flow between the inlet and exhaust sleeves.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"送氣間距過大或壓力不足，遠離送氣口的區段幾乎沒有流量，排氣口讀值卻可能因為近端空氣短路而看似乾燥；壓力過高則超過包覆與索夾密封的承受能力，造成鼓起、剝離與大量洩漏。","textEn":"Spacing too long or pressure too low leaves sections far from the inlet with almost no flow, while exhaust readings may still look dry because air short-circuits near the inlet; pressure too high exceeds what the wrap and band seals can hold, causing bulging, debonding and heavy leakage.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「系統構成與送氣間距」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"System layout and injection spacing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。","送氣間距過大或壓力不足，遠離送氣口的區段幾乎沒有流量，排氣口讀值卻可能因為近端空氣短路而看似乾燥。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.","Spacing too long or pressure too low leaves sections far from the inlet with almost no flow, while exhaust readings may still look dry because air short-circuits near the inlet."],"answer":2,"explanation":"送氣間距過大或壓力不足，遠離送氣口的區段幾乎沒有流量，排氣口讀值卻可能因為近端空氣短路而看似乾燥；壓力過高則超過包覆與索夾密封的承受能力，造成鼓起、剝離與大量洩漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Spacing too long or pressure too low leaves sections far from the inlet with almost no flow, while exhaust readings may still look dry because air short-circuits near the inlet; pressure too high exceeds what the wrap and band seals can hold, causing bulging, debonding and heavy leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b052-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「氣密包覆與索夾密封細部」與「除濕機組容量與預冷設備」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details\" and \"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b052-v13-09","title":"氣密包覆與索夾密封細部：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastomeric wrap and band seals” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"傳統的鍍鋅軟鋼纏絲加防蝕膏與塗裝並不氣密，乾燥空氣會從纏絲縫隙大量逸出。除濕系統因此改用強化彈性體帶材包覆，以重疊纏繞並加熱熔合成連續的氣密外殼；大貝爾特東橋即以 Cableguard 強化彈性體包覆主纜，並在索夾周圍密封。系統的弱點通常不在包覆本身，而在不連續處：索夾兩端、吊索穿出處、送排氣套筒與檢查開口。這些位置要用專用的密封件與填充材，並能承受溫度循環與主纜的微小變形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Traditional soft galvanised wrapping wire with paste and paint is not airtight, and dry air escapes in quantity through its gaps. Dehumidification systems therefore use reinforced elastomeric tape wound with overlaps and heat-fused into a continuous airtight skin; the Great Belt East Bridge was wrapped with Cableguard reinforced elastomer and sealed around its cable clamps. The weak points are usually not the wrap itself but the discontinuities: both ends of each band, hanger exits, injection and exhaust sleeves and inspection openings. These need dedicated seals and fillers that tolerate temperature cycles and small cable movements. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Elastomeric wrap and band seals” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：洩漏口流量 Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Leak flow Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ).","failure":"常見誤解：「包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Elastomeric wrap and band seals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-09-k1","title":"氣密包覆與索夾密封細部","titleEn":"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details","text":"傳統的鍍鋅軟鋼纏絲加防蝕膏與塗裝並不氣密，乾燥空氣會從纏絲縫隙大量逸出。除濕系統因此改用強化彈性體帶材包覆，以重疊纏繞並加熱熔合成連續的氣密外殼；大貝爾特東橋即以 Cableguard 強化彈性體包覆主纜，並在索夾周圍密封。","textEn":"Traditional soft galvanised wrapping wire with paste and paint is not airtight, and dry air escapes in quantity through its gaps. Dehumidification systems therefore use reinforced elastomeric tape wound with overlaps and heat-fused into a continuous airtight skin; the Great Belt East Bridge was wrapped with Cableguard reinforced elastomer and sealed around its cable clamps.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氣密包覆與索夾密封細部」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details\" is correct?","options":["傳統的鍍鋅軟鋼纏絲加防蝕膏與塗裝並不氣密，乾燥空氣會從纏絲縫隙大量逸出。","包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。","除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。"],"optionsEn":["Traditional soft galvanised wrapping wire with paste and paint is not airtight, and dry air escapes in quantity through its gaps.","The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.","Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do."],"answer":0,"explanation":"傳統的鍍鋅軟鋼纏絲加防蝕膏與塗裝並不氣密，乾燥空氣會從纏絲縫隙大量逸出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Traditional soft galvanised wrapping wire with paste and paint is not airtight, and dry air escapes in quantity through its gaps. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b052-v13-10","title":"氣密包覆與索夾密封細部：定量估算","titleEn":"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastomeric wrap and band seals” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：洩漏口流量 Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ)。取 C_d = 0.6、洩漏面積 1 cm²（1×10⁻⁴ m²）、壓差 2,000 Pa、空氣密度 1.2 kg/m³：流速 √(2×2,000/1.2) ≈ 57.7 m/s，Q ≈ 0.6×10⁻⁴×57.7 ≈ 3.5×10⁻³ m³/s（約 208 L/min），比上一單元整段主纜約 27 L/min 的流量大七倍以上。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Leak flow Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ). With C_d = 0.6, a 1 cm² leak (1×10⁻⁴ m²), 2,000 Pa and air density 1.2 kg/m³: velocity √(2×2,000/1.2) ≈ 57.7 m/s and Q ≈ 0.6×10⁻⁴×57.7 ≈ 3.5×10⁻³ m³/s (about 208 L/min), more than seven times the roughly 27 L/min flowing through a whole cable section in the previous unit. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：包覆熔合時記錄環境溫度、濕度、熔合溫度與搭接寬度，抽樣做剝離試驗；每區段完成後封閉做壓力保持試驗，以肥皂水或超音波檢漏器沿索夾邊緣與套筒逐一檢查，修補後再試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During wrap fusion log ambient temperature, humidity, fusion temperature and lap width, with sample peel tests; after each section, seal it for a pressure-hold test and check band edges and sleeves one by one with soapy water or an ultrasonic leak detector, retesting after repair.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"洩漏口流量 Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ)。取 C_d = 0.6、洩漏面積 1 cm²（1×10⁻⁴ m²）、壓差 2,000 Pa、空氣密度 1.2 kg/m³：流速 √(2×2,000/1.2) ≈ 57.7 m/s，Q ≈ 0.6×10⁻⁴×57.7 ≈ 3.5×10⁻³ m³/s（約 208 L/min），比上一單元整段主纜約 27 L/min 的流量大七倍以上。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Leak flow Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ). With C_d = 0.6, a 1 cm² leak (1×10⁻⁴ m²), 2,000 Pa and air density 1.2 kg/m³: velocity √(2×2,000/1.2) ≈ 57.7 m/s and Q ≈ 0.6×10⁻⁴×57.7 ≈ 3.5×10⁻³ m³/s (about 208 L/min), more than seven times the roughly 27 L/min flowing through a whole cable section in the previous unit. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氣密包覆與索夾密封細部」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details\", which statement holds?","options":["除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","洩漏口流量 Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ)。","裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","Leak flow Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ).","Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洩漏口流量 Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Leak flow Q = C_d·A·√(2Δp/ρ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b052-v13-11","title":"氣密包覆與索夾密封細部：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastomeric wrap and band seals” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"包覆熔合時記錄環境溫度、濕度、熔合溫度與搭接寬度，抽樣做剝離試驗；每區段完成後封閉做壓力保持試驗，以肥皂水或超音波檢漏器沿索夾邊緣與套筒逐一檢查，修補後再試驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During wrap fusion log ambient temperature, humidity, fusion temperature and lap width, with sample peel tests; after each section, seal it for a pressure-hold test and check band edges and sleeves one by one with soapy water or an ultrasonic leak detector, retesting after repair. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工規範應規定熔合的環境條件、搭接寬度、索夾與套筒的標準密封細部，以及每區段的氣密驗收；索夾螺栓再張拉、吊索更換或檢查開口後，都必須按同一細部恢復密封並重新試驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification should set environmental limits for fusion, lap width, standard seal details at bands and sleeves and airtightness acceptance per section; after bolt re-tensioning, hanger replacement or inspection openings, the seal must be restored to the same detail and retested.","failure":"注意干擾：一個未密封的索夾端或破損的搭接，就能讓大部分乾燥空氣在近端逸出，下游區段持續潮濕；包覆在低溫或潮濕時熔合，日後在溫度循環下沿搭接開裂，雨水反而從裂縫進入。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One unsealed band end or broken lap can vent most of the dry air near the inlet while downstream sections stay damp; wrap fused in cold or wet weather can split along laps under later thermal cycles, letting rain in through the cracks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"包覆熔合時記錄環境溫度、濕度、熔合溫度與搭接寬度，抽樣做剝離試驗；每區段完成後封閉做壓力保持試驗，以肥皂水或超音波檢漏器沿索夾邊緣與套筒逐一檢查，修補後再試驗。","textEn":"During wrap fusion log ambient temperature, humidity, fusion temperature and lap width, with sample peel tests; after each section, seal it for a pressure-hold test and check band edges and sleeves one by one with soapy water or an ultrasonic leak detector, retesting after repair.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工規範應規定熔合的環境條件、搭接寬度、索夾與套筒的標準密封細部，以及每區段的氣密驗收；索夾螺栓再張拉、吊索更換或檢查開口後，都必須按同一細部恢復密封並重新試驗。","textEn":"The specification should set environmental limits for fusion, lap width, standard seal details at bands and sleeves and airtightness acceptance per section; after bolt re-tensioning, hanger replacement or inspection openings, the seal must be restored to the same detail and retested.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氣密包覆與索夾密封細部」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。","包覆熔合時記錄環境溫度、濕度、熔合溫度與搭接寬度，抽樣做剝離試驗；每區段完成後封閉做壓力保持試驗，以肥皂水或超音波檢漏器沿索夾邊緣與套筒逐一檢查，修補後再試驗。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money.","During wrap fusion log ambient temperature, humidity, fusion temperature and lap width, with sample peel tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"包覆熔合時記錄環境溫度、濕度、熔合溫度與搭接寬度，抽樣做剝離試驗；每區段完成後封閉做壓力保持試驗，以肥皂水或超音波檢漏器沿索夾邊緣與套筒逐一檢查，修補後再試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During wrap fusion log ambient temperature, humidity, fusion temperature and lap width, with sample peel tests; after each section, seal it for a pressure-hold test and check band edges and sleeves one by one with soapy water or an ultrasonic leak detector, retesting after repair. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b052-v13-12","title":"氣密包覆與索夾密封細部：失效診斷","titleEn":"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彈性體包覆與索夾密封」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastomeric wrap and band seals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一個未密封的索夾端或破損的搭接，就能讓大部分乾燥空氣在近端逸出，下游區段持續潮濕；包覆在低溫或潮濕時熔合，日後在溫度循環下沿搭接開裂，雨水反而從裂縫進入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One unsealed band end or broken lap can vent most of the dry air near the inlet while downstream sections stay damp; wrap fused in cold or wet weather can split along laps under later thermal cycles, letting rain in through the cracks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些位置要用專用的密封件與填充材，並能承受溫度循環與主纜的微小變形。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: These need dedicated seals and fillers that tolerate temperature cycles and small cable movements.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一個未密封的索夾端或破損的搭接，就能讓大部分乾燥空氣在近端逸出，下游區段持續潮濕；包覆在低溫或潮濕時熔合，日後在溫度循環下沿搭接開裂，雨水反而從裂縫進入。","textEn":"One unsealed band end or broken lap can vent most of the dry air near the inlet while downstream sections stay damp; wrap fused in cold or wet weather can split along laps under later thermal cycles, letting rain in through the cracks.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氣密包覆與索夾密封細部」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Airtight wrapping and cable-band seal details\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["一個未密封的索夾端或破損的搭接，就能讓大部分乾燥空氣在近端逸出，下游區段持續潮濕；包覆在低溫或潮濕時熔合，日後在溫度循環下沿搭接開裂，雨水反而從裂縫進入。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。"],"optionsEn":["One unsealed band end or broken lap can vent most of the dry air near the inlet while downstream sections stay damp.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一個未密封的索夾端或破損的搭接，就能讓大部分乾燥空氣在近端逸出，下游區段持續潮濕；包覆在低溫或潮濕時熔合，日後在溫度循環下沿搭接開裂，雨水反而從裂縫進入。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One unsealed band end or broken lap can vent most of the dry air near the inlet while downstream sections stay damp; wrap fused in cold or wet weather can split along laps under later thermal cycles, letting rain in through the cracks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b052-v13-13","title":"除濕機組容量與預冷設備：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「除濕機與預冷」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜除濕常用吸附式除濕機：空氣通過含吸濕劑的轉輪，水氣被吸附，轉輪另一側以加熱空氣再生，把水分排到外面。吸附式在低溫下仍能產生很低露點的空氣，適合送入主纜。本州四國連絡橋在夏季高濕時加裝預冷設備，先以冷卻盤管把外氣降溫凝結出一部分水，再送入除濕機，減輕轉輪負荷。機組容量必須依最不利季節的外氣條件、總送氣量與目標送氣濕度決定，並保留備援。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「除濕機與預冷」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cable systems commonly use desiccant dehumidifiers: air passes through a rotor carrying a desiccant that adsorbs vapour, while the other side of the rotor is regenerated with heated air that carries the moisture outside. Desiccant units deliver very low dew-point air even at low temperatures, which suits cable injection. The Honshu-Shikoku bridges added pre-coolers for humid summers: cooling coils lower outdoor air temperature and condense part of its water before it reaches the dehumidifier, easing the load on the rotor. Unit capacity must be set from outdoor air in the worst season, total supply flow and target supply humidity, with redundancy. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：水氣密度：30 °C、80% RH 約 24.2 g/m³；25 °C、20% RH 約 4.6 g/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Vapour density: about 24.2 g/m³ at 30 °C and 80% RH, about 4.6 g/m³ at 25 °C and 20% RH.","failure":"常見誤解：「除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「除濕機與預冷」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-13-k1","title":"除濕機組容量與預冷設備","titleEn":"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers","text":"主纜除濕常用吸附式除濕機：空氣通過含吸濕劑的轉輪，水氣被吸附，轉輪另一側以加熱空氣再生，把水分排到外面。吸附式在低溫下仍能產生很低露點的空氣，適合送入主纜。","textEn":"Cable systems commonly use desiccant dehumidifiers: air passes through a rotor carrying a desiccant that adsorbs vapour, while the other side of the rotor is regenerated with heated air that carries the moisture outside. Desiccant units deliver very low dew-point air even at low temperatures, which suits cable injection.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「除濕機組容量與預冷設備」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers\" is correct?","options":["除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。","主纜除濕常用吸附式除濕機：空氣通過含吸濕劑的轉輪，水氣被吸附，轉輪另一側以加熱空氣再生，把水分排到外面。","除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。"],"optionsEn":["Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do.","Cable systems commonly use desiccant dehumidifiers: air passes through a rotor carrying a desiccant that adsorbs vapour, while the other side of the rotor is regenerated with heated air that carries the moisture outside.","A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜除濕常用吸附式除濕機：空氣通過含吸濕劑的轉輪，水氣被吸附，轉輪另一側以加熱空氣再生，把水分排到外面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cable systems commonly use desiccant dehumidifiers: air passes through a rotor carrying a desiccant that adsorbs vapour, while the other side of the rotor is regenerated with heated air that carries the moisture outside. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b052-v13-14","title":"除濕機組容量與預冷設備：定量估算","titleEn":"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「除濕機與預冷」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：水氣密度：30 °C、80% RH 約 24.2 g/m³；25 °C、20% RH 約 4.6 g/m³。每立方公尺需除去約 19.6 g，送氣 10 m³/min 時約 11.8 kg/h。若先預冷到 15 °C 飽和（約 12.8 g/m³），凝結去除約 11.4 g/m³，吸附轉輪只需處理約 8.2 g/m³，即原負荷的約 42%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Vapour density: about 24.2 g/m³ at 30 °C and 80% RH, about 4.6 g/m³ at 25 °C and 20% RH. Each cubic metre must lose about 19.6 g, about 11.8 kg/h at 10 m³/min. Pre-cooling to saturation at 15 °C (about 12.8 g/m³) condenses about 11.4 g/m³, leaving the desiccant rotor only about 8.2 g/m³, about 42% of the original load. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：工廠驗收時量測機組在多種進氣溫濕度下的出氣露點與流量，確認符合規格曲線；現場以進、出口溫濕度與流量計算實際除濕量，與設計值比較，並記錄再生溫度與轉輪轉速，作為日後性能退化的基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At factory acceptance measure outlet dew point and flow over a range of inlet conditions against the specification curve; on site compute actual moisture removal from inlet and outlet humidity and flow, compare with design, and record regeneration temperature and rotor speed as the baseline for later degradation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"水氣密度：30 °C、80% RH 約 24.2 g/m³；25 °C、20% RH 約 4.6 g/m³。每立方公尺需除去約 19.6 g，送氣 10 m³/min 時約 11.8 kg/h。若先預冷到 15 °C 飽和（約 12.8 g/m³），凝結去除約 11.4 g/m³，吸附轉輪只需處理約 8.2 g/m³，即原負荷的約 42%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Vapour density: about 24.2 g/m³ at 30 °C and 80% RH, about 4.6 g/m³ at 25 °C and 20% RH. Each cubic metre must lose about 19.6 g, about 11.8 kg/h at 10 m³/min. Pre-cooling to saturation at 15 °C (about 12.8 g/m³) condenses about 11.4 g/m³, leaving the desiccant rotor only about 8.2 g/m³, about 42% of the original load. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「除濕機組容量與預冷設備」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers\", which statement holds?","options":["只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。","除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。","水氣密度：30 °C、80% RH 約 24.2 g/m³；25 °C、20% RH 約 4.6 g/m³。"],"optionsEn":["If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation.","Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.","Vapour density: about 24.2 g/m³ at 30 °C and 80% RH, about 4.6 g/m³ at 25 °C and 20% RH."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水氣密度：30 °C、80% RH 約 24.2 g/m³；25 °C、20% RH 約 4.6 g/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Vapour density: about 24.2 g/m³ at 30 °C and 80% RH, about 4.6 g/m³ at 25 °C and 20% RH. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b052-v13-15","title":"除濕機組容量與預冷設備：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「除濕機與預冷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"工廠驗收時量測機組在多種進氣溫濕度下的出氣露點與流量，確認符合規格曲線；現場以進、出口溫濕度與流量計算實際除濕量，與設計值比較，並記錄再生溫度與轉輪轉速，作為日後性能退化的基準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At factory acceptance measure outlet dew point and flow over a range of inlet conditions against the specification curve; on site compute actual moisture removal from inlet and outlet humidity and flow, compare with design, and record regeneration temperature and rotor speed as the baseline for later degradation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：採購規範應以設計外氣條件、送氣露點、流量、備援數量、遠端監控介面與維修可及性定義機組；機房位置要考慮維修人員的安全通道與設備吊運路線，並保留更換整台機組的空間。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define units in the procurement specification by design outdoor conditions, supply dew point, flow, redundancy, remote-monitoring interface and maintainability; locate plant rooms with safe access for maintenance staff and a lifting route, leaving space to replace a complete unit.","failure":"注意干擾：若以年平均氣候選機，夏季高濕時送氣濕度超標，纜內濕度回升；機組單點故障而無備援，維修期間整段主纜停止送氣；預冷盤管凝結水排放不良則可能結冰或回流進送氣管。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing units on annual-average climate lets supply humidity exceed target in humid summers so cable humidity climbs; a single unit failing without redundancy stops injection to a whole section during repair; poor condensate drainage from pre-cooler coils can freeze or run back into the supply duct. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"工廠驗收時量測機組在多種進氣溫濕度下的出氣露點與流量，確認符合規格曲線；現場以進、出口溫濕度與流量計算實際除濕量，與設計值比較，並記錄再生溫度與轉輪轉速，作為日後性能退化的基準。","textEn":"At factory acceptance measure outlet dew point and flow over a range of inlet conditions against the specification curve; on site compute actual moisture removal from inlet and outlet humidity and flow, compare with design, and record regeneration temperature and rotor speed as the baseline for later degradation.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"採購規範應以設計外氣條件、送氣露點、流量、備援數量、遠端監控介面與維修可及性定義機組；機房位置要考慮維修人員的安全通道與設備吊運路線，並保留更換整台機組的空間。","textEn":"Define units in the procurement specification by design outdoor conditions, supply dew point, flow, redundancy, remote-monitoring interface and maintainability; locate plant rooms with safe access for maintenance staff and a lifting route, leaving space to replace a complete unit.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「除濕機組容量與預冷設備」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers\"?","options":["工廠驗收時量測機組在多種進氣溫濕度下的出氣露點與流量，確認符合規格曲線。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。"],"optionsEn":["At factory acceptance measure outlet dew point and flow over a range of inlet conditions against the specification curve.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside."],"answer":0,"explanation":"工廠驗收時量測機組在多種進氣溫濕度下的出氣露點與流量，確認符合規格曲線；現場以進、出口溫濕度與流量計算實際除濕量，與設計值比較，並記錄再生溫度與轉輪轉速，作為日後性能退化的基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At factory acceptance measure outlet dew point and flow over a range of inlet conditions against the specification curve; on site compute actual moisture removal from inlet and outlet humidity and flow, compare with design, and record regeneration temperature and rotor speed as the baseline for later degradation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b052-v13-16","title":"除濕機組容量與預冷設備：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「除濕機與預冷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dehumidifier and pre-cooler” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若以年平均氣候選機，夏季高濕時送氣濕度超標，纜內濕度回升；機組單點故障而無備援，維修期間整段主纜停止送氣；預冷盤管凝結水排放不良則可能結冰或回流進送氣管。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing units on annual-average climate lets supply humidity exceed target in humid summers so cable humidity climbs; a single unit failing without redundancy stops injection to a whole section during repair; poor condensate drainage from pre-cooler coils can freeze or run back into the supply duct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：機組容量必須依最不利季節的外氣條件、總送氣量與目標送氣濕度決定，並保留備援。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Unit capacity must be set from outdoor air in the worst season, total supply flow and target supply humidity, with redundancy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若以年平均氣候選機，夏季高濕時送氣濕度超標，纜內濕度回升；機組單點故障而無備援，維修期間整段主纜停止送氣；預冷盤管凝結水排放不良則可能結冰或回流進送氣管。","textEn":"Sizing units on annual-average climate lets supply humidity exceed target in humid summers so cable humidity climbs; a single unit failing without redundancy stops injection to a whole section during repair; poor condensate drainage from pre-cooler coils can freeze or run back into the supply duct.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「除濕機組容量與預冷設備」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dehumidifier capacity and pre-coolers\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若以年平均氣候選機，夏季高濕時送氣濕度超標，纜內濕度回升；機組單點故障而無備援，維修期間整段主纜停止送氣；預冷盤管凝結水排放不良則可能結冰或回流進送氣管。","除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Sizing units on annual-average climate lets supply humidity exceed target in humid summers so cable humidity climbs.","A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若以年平均氣候選機，夏季高濕時送氣濕度超標，纜內濕度回升；機組單點故障而無備援，維修期間整段主纜停止送氣；預冷盤管凝結水排放不良則可能結冰或回流進送氣管。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing units on annual-average climate lets supply humidity exceed target in humid summers so cable humidity climbs; a single unit failing without redundancy stops injection to a whole section during repair; poor condensate drainage from pre-cooler coils can freeze or run back into the supply duct. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b052-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「既有主纜的除濕改造施工」與「啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable\" and \"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b052-v13-17","title":"既有主纜的除濕改造施工：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「既有主纜改造順序」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Retrofit sequence on a live cable” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大貝爾特東橋的主纜除濕系統於 2014 年開始安裝、2015 年 9 月完成，是在橋梁持續通車下進行的改造。典型流程是：清理既有纏絲與塗裝表面、修補局部損傷，在索夾兩端與吊索處安裝密封件，在選定位置安裝送氣與排氣套筒，然後以彈性體帶材沿主纜纏繞並熱熔，最後連接送氣管、機組與感測器。作業沿主纜在臨時平台或纜上移動式設備上進行，進度受風、雨與溫度限制，因為熔合需要乾燥表面與足夠溫度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「既有主纜改造順序」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Great Belt East Bridge cable dehumidification system was installed from 2014 and completed in September 2015 while the bridge stayed open. A typical sequence is to clean the existing wrapping and paint, repair local damage, fit seals at both ends of each band and at hanger exits, install injection and exhaust sleeves at chosen positions, wind and heat-fuse elastomeric tape along the cable, then connect ducts, units and sensors. Work proceeds along the cable from temporary platforms or travelling equipment, and progress is limited by wind, rain and temperature, because fusion needs a dry surface and enough warmth. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Retrofit sequence on a live cable” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：兩條各約 3 km 的主纜共 6,000 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Two cables of about 3 km each make 6,000 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「既有主纜改造順序」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Retrofit sequence on a live cable”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-17-k1","title":"既有主纜的除濕改造施工","titleEn":"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable","text":"大貝爾特東橋的主纜除濕系統於 2014 年開始安裝、2015 年 9 月完成，是在橋梁持續通車下進行的改造。典型流程是：清理既有纏絲與塗裝表面、修補局部損傷，在索夾兩端與吊索處安裝密封件，在選定位置安裝送氣與排氣套筒，然後以彈性體帶材沿主纜纏繞並熱熔，最後連接送氣管、機組與感測器。","textEn":"The Great Belt East Bridge cable dehumidification system was installed from 2014 and completed in September 2015 while the bridge stayed open. A typical sequence is to clean the existing wrapping and paint, repair local damage, fit seals at both ends of each band and at hanger exits, install injection and exhaust sleeves at chosen positions, wind and heat-fuse elastomeric tape along the cable, then connect ducts, units and sensors.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「既有主纜的除濕改造施工」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable\" is correct?","options":["除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。","除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","大貝爾特東橋的主纜除濕系統於 2014 年開始安裝、2015 年 9 月完成，是在橋梁持續通車下進行的改造。"],"optionsEn":["A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather.","Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","The Great Belt East Bridge cable dehumidification system was installed from 2014 and completed in September 2015 while the bridge stayed open."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大貝爾特東橋的主纜除濕系統於 2014 年開始安裝、2015 年 9 月完成，是在橋梁持續通車下進行的改造。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Great Belt East Bridge cable dehumidification system was installed from 2014 and completed in September 2015 while the bridge stayed open. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b052-v13-18","title":"既有主纜的除濕改造施工：定量估算","titleEn":"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「既有主纜改造順序」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Retrofit sequence on a live cable” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：兩條各約 3 km 的主纜共 6,000 m。若每組人員每日可完成 40 m 包覆，需 6,000/40 = 150 組日；4 組同時作業約 37.5 個可施工日。若只有 50% 的日子符合熔合的天候條件，約需 75 個日曆天，尚未計入套筒與索夾密封。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Two cables of about 3 km each make 6,000 m. At 40 m of wrapping per crew per day, the job needs 6,000/40 = 150 crew-days; with 4 crews working together, about 37.5 workable days. If only 50% of days meet the weather conditions for fusion, it takes about 75 calendar days, before sleeves and band seals are added. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每日記錄施工區段、天候、熔合參數與完成長度，對未達條件的日子停止熔合；每完成一個送排氣區段就做氣密試驗，合格後才能進入下一段；纜上設備的荷重、錨固與防墜措施由臨時工程設計者核可。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Log section, weather, fusion parameters and length completed each day, stopping fusion when conditions are not met; test each injection–exhaust section for airtightness before moving on; have the temporary-works designer approve loads, anchorage and fall protection of on-cable equipment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"兩條各約 3 km 的主纜共 6,000 m。若每組人員每日可完成 40 m 包覆，需 6,000/40 = 150 組日；4 組同時作業約 37.5 個可施工日。若只有 50% 的日子符合熔合的天候條件，約需 75 個日曆天，尚未計入套筒與索夾密封。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Two cables of about 3 km each make 6,000 m. At 40 m of wrapping per crew per day, the job needs 6,000/40 = 150 crew-days; with 4 crews working together, about 37.5 workable days. If only 50% of days meet the weather conditions for fusion, it takes about 75 calendar days, before sleeves and band seals are added. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「既有主纜的除濕改造施工」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable\", which statement holds?","options":["兩條各約 3 km 的主纜共 6,000 m。","裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。","主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。"],"optionsEn":["Two cables of about 3 km each make 6,000 m.","Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again.","Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩條各約 3 km 的主纜共 6,000 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Two cables of about 3 km each make 6,000 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b052-v13-19","title":"既有主纜的除濕改造施工：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「既有主纜改造順序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Retrofit sequence on a live cable” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每日記錄施工區段、天候、熔合參數與完成長度，對未達條件的日子停止熔合；每完成一個送排氣區段就做氣密試驗，合格後才能進入下一段；纜上設備的荷重、錨固與防墜措施由臨時工程設計者核可。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Log section, weather, fusion parameters and length completed each day, stopping fusion when conditions are not met; test each injection–exhaust section for airtightness before moving on; have the temporary-works designer approve loads, anchorage and fall protection of on-cable equipment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：改造合約應把天候限制、熔合參數、逐段氣密試驗與纜上作業安全列為停留點，並要求承包商提交每日紀錄；交通管制與高空作業許可由業主統一協調，任何設備附掛在主纜上都需要結構工程師核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The retrofit contract should make weather limits, fusion parameters, section-by-section airtightness tests and safety of work on the cable hold points, with daily records from the contractor; the owner coordinates traffic management and work-at-height permits, and anything attached to the cable needs the structural engineer's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：為趕進度在潮濕或低溫天候熔合，搭接黏結不良，系統啟動後才發現大量洩漏；清理不完全時，既有塗料或防蝕膏夾在包覆下方，影響黏結並可能積水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fusing in damp or cold weather to catch up leaves weak laps that leak heavily once the system starts; incomplete cleaning traps old paint or paste under the wrap, spoiling adhesion and possibly holding water; poorly secured on-cable equipment can also scratch the wrap or wrapping wire. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每日記錄施工區段、天候、熔合參數與完成長度，對未達條件的日子停止熔合；每完成一個送排氣區段就做氣密試驗，合格後才能進入下一段；纜上設備的荷重、錨固與防墜措施由臨時工程設計者核可。","textEn":"Log section, weather, fusion parameters and length completed each day, stopping fusion when conditions are not met; test each injection–exhaust section for airtightness before moving on; have the temporary-works designer approve loads, anchorage and fall protection of on-cable equipment.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"改造合約應把天候限制、熔合參數、逐段氣密試驗與纜上作業安全列為停留點，並要求承包商提交每日紀錄；交通管制與高空作業許可由業主統一協調，任何設備附掛在主纜上都需要結構工程師核可。","textEn":"The retrofit contract should make weather limits, fusion parameters, section-by-section airtightness tests and safety of work on the cable hold points, with daily records from the contractor; the owner coordinates traffic management and work-at-height permits, and anything attached to the cable needs the structural engineer's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「既有主纜的除濕改造施工」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每日記錄施工區段、天候、熔合參數與完成長度，對未達條件的日子停止熔合。","只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Log section, weather, fusion parameters and length completed each day, stopping fusion when conditions are not met.","Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每日記錄施工區段、天候、熔合參數與完成長度，對未達條件的日子停止熔合；每完成一個送排氣區段就做氣密試驗，合格後才能進入下一段；纜上設備的荷重、錨固與防墜措施由臨時工程設計者核可。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Log section, weather, fusion parameters and length completed each day, stopping fusion when conditions are not met; test each injection–exhaust section for airtightness before moving on; have the temporary-works designer approve loads, anchorage and fall protection of on-cable equipment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b052-v13-20","title":"既有主纜的除濕改造施工：失效診斷","titleEn":"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「既有主纜改造順序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Retrofit sequence on a live cable” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為趕進度在潮濕或低溫天候熔合，搭接黏結不良，系統啟動後才發現大量洩漏；清理不完全時，既有塗料或防蝕膏夾在包覆下方，影響黏結並可能積水。纜上設備若固定不當，也可能刮傷包覆或纏絲。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fusing in damp or cold weather to catch up leaves weak laps that leak heavily once the system starts; incomplete cleaning traps old paint or paste under the wrap, spoiling adhesion and possibly holding water; poorly secured on-cable equipment can also scratch the wrap or wrapping wire. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：作業沿主纜在臨時平台或纜上移動式設備上進行，進度受風、雨與溫度限制，因為熔合需要乾燥表面與足夠溫度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Work proceeds along the cable from temporary platforms or travelling equipment, and progress is limited by wind, rain and temperature, because fusion needs a dry surface and enough warmth.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為趕進度在潮濕或低溫天候熔合，搭接黏結不良，系統啟動後才發現大量洩漏；清理不完全時，既有塗料或防蝕膏夾在包覆下方，影響黏結並可能積水。纜上設備若固定不當，也可能刮傷包覆或纏絲。","textEn":"Fusing in damp or cold weather to catch up leaves weak laps that leak heavily once the system starts; incomplete cleaning traps old paint or paste under the wrap, spoiling adhesion and possibly holding water; poorly secured on-cable equipment can also scratch the wrap or wrapping wire.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「既有主纜的除濕改造施工」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Retrofitting dehumidification to an existing cable\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","為趕進度在潮濕或低溫天候熔合，搭接黏結不良，系統啟動後才發現大量洩漏；清理不完全時，既有塗料或防蝕膏夾在包覆下方，影響黏結並可能積水。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","Fusing in damp or cold weather to catch up leaves weak laps that leak heavily once the system starts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為趕進度在潮濕或低溫天候熔合，搭接黏結不良，系統啟動後才發現大量洩漏；清理不完全時，既有塗料或防蝕膏夾在包覆下方，影響黏結並可能積水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fusing in damp or cold weather to catch up leaves weak laps that leak heavily once the system starts; incomplete cleaning traps old paint or paste under the wrap, spoiling adhesion and possibly holding water; poorly secured on-cable equipment can also scratch the wrap or wrapping wire. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b052-v13-21","title":"啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「啟動乾燥曲線」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Start-up dry-out curve” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"系統啟動時，主纜內可能有多年累積的水分，排氣口的相對濕度一開始接近飽和，隨著殘留水分被帶走而逐漸下降，最後趨近由送氣濕度與持續滲入量決定的穩定值。下降曲線通常近似指數衰減，時間常數取決於殘留水量、送氣流量與水分從鋼絲間隙蒸發的速度。本州四國連絡橋以 40% RH 為管理目標，比會發生腐蝕的約 60% 留有餘裕；調試時就是看排氣濕度何時、能否穩定落在目標以下。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「啟動乾燥曲線」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At start-up the cable may hold years of accumulated moisture, so exhaust relative humidity begins near saturation, falls as trapped water is carried away and finally approaches a steady value set by supply humidity and continuing ingress. The decline is usually close to exponential, with a time constant set by the amount of trapped water, supply flow and how fast water evaporates from the wire interstices. The Honshu-Shikoku bridges manage to 40% RH, a margin below the roughly 60% at which corrosion occurs; commissioning watches when, and whether, exhaust humidity settles below that target. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Start-up dry-out curve” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ).","failure":"常見誤解：「除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「啟動乾燥曲線」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Start-up dry-out curve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-21-k1","title":"啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減","titleEn":"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay","text":"系統啟動時，主纜內可能有多年累積的水分，排氣口的相對濕度一開始接近飽和，隨著殘留水分被帶走而逐漸下降，最後趨近由送氣濕度與持續滲入量決定的穩定值。下降曲線通常近似指數衰減，時間常數取決於殘留水量、送氣流量與水分從鋼絲間隙蒸發的速度。","textEn":"At start-up the cable may hold years of accumulated moisture, so exhaust relative humidity begins near saturation, falls as trapped water is carried away and finally approaches a steady value set by supply humidity and continuing ingress. The decline is usually close to exponential, with a time constant set by the amount of trapped water, supply flow and how fast water evaporates from the wire interstices.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay\" is correct?","options":["系統啟動時，主纜內可能有多年累積的水分，排氣口的相對濕度一開始接近飽和，隨著殘留水分被帶走而逐漸下降，最後趨近由送氣濕度與持續滲入量決定的穩定值。","除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。"],"optionsEn":["At start-up the cable may hold years of accumulated moisture, so exhaust relative humidity begins near saturation, falls as trapped water is carried away and finally approaches a steady value set by supply humidity and continuing ingress.","Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"系統啟動時，主纜內可能有多年累積的水分，排氣口的相對濕度一開始接近飽和，隨著殘留水分被帶走而逐漸下降，最後趨近由送氣濕度與持續滲入量決定的穩定值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At start-up the cable may hold years of accumulated moisture, so exhaust relative humidity begins near saturation, falls as trapped water is carried away and finally approaches a steady value set by supply humidity and continuing ingress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b052-v13-22","title":"啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減：定量估算","titleEn":"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「啟動乾燥曲線」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Start-up dry-out curve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ)。取 RH₀ = 90%、RH_∞ = 30%、τ = 20 天：降到 40% 所需 t = τ·ln[(90 − 30)/(40 − 30)] = 20×ln 6 ≈ 35.8 天。若某區段 τ 實測為 40 天，則需約 72 天；若 RH_∞ 高於 40%，曲線永遠到不了目標。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ). With RH₀ = 90%, RH_∞ = 30% and τ = 20 days, reaching 40% takes t = τ·ln[(90 − 30)/(40 − 30)] = 20×ln 6 ≈ 35.8 days. A section with a measured τ of 40 days needs about 72 days; if RH_∞ is above 40%, the curve never reaches the target. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個區段從啟動起逐日記錄排氣溫濕度與流量，以指數曲線擬合 τ 與 RH_∞，預測達標日期；擬合的 RH_∞ 高於目標的區段，優先檢查洩漏、送氣量與局部積水，必要時開窗排水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: From start-up log exhaust humidity, temperature and flow daily for each section, fit τ and RH_∞ to an exponential curve and forecast the date of reaching target; for sections whose fitted RH_∞ exceeds the target, check leaks, supply flow and local standing water first, opening a window to drain if needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ)。取 RH₀ = 90%、RH_∞ = 30%、τ = 20 天：降到 40% 所需 t = τ·ln[(90 − 30)/(40 − 30)] = 20×ln 6 ≈ 35.8 天。若某區段 τ 實測為 40 天，則需約 72 天；若 RH_∞ 高於 40%，曲線永遠到不了目標。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ). With RH₀ = 90%, RH_∞ = 30% and τ = 20 days, reaching 40% takes t = τ·ln[(90 − 30)/(40 − 30)] = 20×ln 6 ≈ 35.8 days. A section with a measured τ of 40 days needs about 72 days; if RH_∞ is above 40%, the curve never reaches the target. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay\", which statement holds?","options":["除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。","RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ)。","主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。"],"optionsEn":["Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.","RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ).","With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"RH(t) = RH_∞ + (RH₀ − RH_∞)·e^(−t/τ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b052-v13-23","title":"啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「啟動乾燥曲線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Start-up dry-out curve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個區段從啟動起逐日記錄排氣溫濕度與流量，以指數曲線擬合 τ 與 RH_∞，預測達標日期；擬合的 RH_∞ 高於目標的區段，優先檢查洩漏、送氣量與局部積水，必要時開窗排水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"From start-up log exhaust humidity, temperature and flow daily for each section, fit τ and RH_∞ to an exponential curve and forecast the date of reaching target; for sections whose fitted RH_∞ exceeds the target, check leaks, supply flow and local standing water first, opening a window to drain if needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：調試規範應定義每個區段的達標準則（例如連續 30 天排氣濕度低於目標）、擬合方法與未達標時的處理流程；調試紀錄與擬合參數納入交接文件，作為日後判斷性能退化的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: The commissioning specification should define the success criterion per section, for example 30 consecutive days of exhaust humidity below target, the fitting method and the procedure when targets are missed; commissioning records and fitted parameters go into the handover file as the baseline for judging later degradation.","failure":"注意干擾：若調試只看最初幾天的下降就宣告完成，可能遺漏下降停滯在目標以上的區段；排氣濕度長期偏高卻被歸因於天候，延誤找出洩漏或積水點，主纜持續在潮濕狀態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Declaring commissioning complete after a few days of decline can miss sections that stall above target; blaming persistently high exhaust humidity on weather delays finding leaks or standing water, and the cable stays damp. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個區段從啟動起逐日記錄排氣溫濕度與流量，以指數曲線擬合 τ 與 RH_∞，預測達標日期；擬合的 RH_∞ 高於目標的區段，優先檢查洩漏、送氣量與局部積水，必要時開窗排水。","textEn":"From start-up log exhaust humidity, temperature and flow daily for each section, fit τ and RH_∞ to an exponential curve and forecast the date of reaching target; for sections whose fitted RH_∞ exceeds the target, check leaks, supply flow and local standing water first, opening a window to drain if needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"調試規範應定義每個區段的達標準則（例如連續 30 天排氣濕度低於目標）、擬合方法與未達標時的處理流程；調試紀錄與擬合參數納入交接文件，作為日後判斷性能退化的基準。","textEn":"The commissioning specification should define the success criterion per section, for example 30 consecutive days of exhaust humidity below target, the fitting method and the procedure when targets are missed; commissioning records and fitted parameters go into the handover file as the baseline for judging later degradation.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。","每個區段從啟動起逐日記錄排氣溫濕度與流量，以指數曲線擬合 τ 與 RH_∞，預測達標日期。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.","From start-up log exhaust humidity, temperature and flow daily for each section, fit τ and RH_∞ to an exponential curve and forecast the date of reaching target."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每個區段從啟動起逐日記錄排氣溫濕度與流量，以指數曲線擬合 τ 與 RH_∞，預測達標日期；擬合的 RH_∞ 高於目標的區段，優先檢查洩漏、送氣量與局部積水，必要時開窗排水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"From start-up log exhaust humidity, temperature and flow daily for each section, fit τ and RH_∞ to an exponential curve and forecast the date of reaching target; for sections whose fitted RH_∞ exceeds the target, check leaks, supply flow and local standing water first, opening a window to drain if needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b052-v13-24","title":"啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減：失效診斷","titleEn":"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「啟動乾燥曲線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Start-up dry-out curve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若調試只看最初幾天的下降就宣告完成，可能遺漏下降停滯在目標以上的區段；排氣濕度長期偏高卻被歸因於天候，延誤找出洩漏或積水點，主纜持續在潮濕狀態。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Declaring commissioning complete after a few days of decline can miss sections that stall above target; blaming persistently high exhaust humidity on weather delays finding leaks or standing water, and the cable stays damp. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本州四國連絡橋以 40% RH 為管理目標，比會發生腐蝕的約 60% 留有餘裕；調試時就是看排氣濕度何時、能否穩定落在目標以下。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Honshu-Shikoku bridges manage to 40% RH, a margin below the roughly 60% at which corrosion occurs; commissioning watches when, and whether, exhaust humidity settles below that target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若調試只看最初幾天的下降就宣告完成，可能遺漏下降停滯在目標以上的區段；排氣濕度長期偏高卻被歸因於天候，延誤找出洩漏或積水點，主纜持續在潮濕狀態。","textEn":"Declaring commissioning complete after a few days of decline can miss sections that stall above target; blaming persistently high exhaust humidity on weather delays finding leaks or standing water, and the cable stays damp.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「啟動乾燥與排氣濕度衰減」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Start-up dry-out and exhaust humidity decay\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若調試只看最初幾天的下降就宣告完成，可能遺漏下降停滯在目標以上的區段；排氣濕度長期偏高卻被歸因於天候，延誤找出洩漏或積水點，主纜持續在潮濕狀態。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。"],"optionsEn":["Declaring commissioning complete after a few days of decline can miss sections that stall above target.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若調試只看最初幾天的下降就宣告完成，可能遺漏下降停滯在目標以上的區段；排氣濕度長期偏高卻被歸因於天候，延誤找出洩漏或積水點，主纜持續在潮濕狀態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Declaring commissioning complete after a few days of decline can miss sections that stall above target; blaming persistently high exhaust humidity on weather delays finding leaks or standing water, and the cable stays damp. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b052-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「感測器網路與露點裕度判讀」與「成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sensor network and dew-point margin\" and \"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b052-v13-25","title":"感測器網路與露點裕度判讀：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Sensor network and dew-point margin: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「排氣溫濕度感測器」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exhaust humidity sensors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"除濕系統的效果只能透過量測看見，感測器至少包括各送氣口與排氣口的溫度、相對濕度與流量，以及代表性位置的鋼絲表面溫度。電容式濕度感測器會隨時間漂移，在高濕或含鹽環境下更快，因此需要定期校正或以可攜式參考儀比對。判讀時不應只看相對濕度，而要把空氣露點與鋼絲溫度比較：相對濕度看似達標，若夜間鋼絲溫度接近露點，仍可能結露。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「排氣溫濕度感測器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The effect of a dehumidification system can only be seen through measurement: at minimum temperature, relative humidity and flow at each injection and exhaust point, plus wire-surface temperature at representative locations. Capacitive humidity sensors drift with time, faster in humid or salty conditions, so they need periodic calibration or comparison with a portable reference. Interpretation should not rest on relative humidity alone but compare air dew point with wire temperature: humidity may look on target while night-time wire temperature approaches the dew point and condensation still occurs. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Exhaust humidity sensors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：排氣空氣 20 °C、40% RH 時露點約 6.0 °C；若夜間鋼絲 8 °C，裕度約 2.0 °C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Exhaust air at 20 °C and 40% RH has a dew point of about 6.0 °C; with wires at 8 °C at night the margin is about 2.0 °C.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「排氣溫濕度感測器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Exhaust humidity sensors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-25-k1","title":"感測器網路與露點裕度判讀","titleEn":"Sensor network and dew-point margin","text":"除濕系統的效果只能透過量測看見，感測器至少包括各送氣口與排氣口的溫度、相對濕度與流量，以及代表性位置的鋼絲表面溫度。電容式濕度感測器會隨時間漂移，在高濕或含鹽環境下更快，因此需要定期校正或以可攜式參考儀比對。","textEn":"The effect of a dehumidification system can only be seen through measurement: at minimum temperature, relative humidity and flow at each injection and exhaust point, plus wire-surface temperature at representative locations. Capacitive humidity sensors drift with time, faster in humid or salty conditions, so they need periodic calibration or comparison with a portable reference.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「感測器網路與露點裕度判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sensor network and dew-point margin\" is correct?","options":["只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。","除濕系統的效果只能透過量測看見，感測器至少包括各送氣口與排氣口的溫度、相對濕度與流量，以及代表性位置的鋼絲表面溫度。","裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。"],"optionsEn":["If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation.","The effect of a dehumidification system can only be seen through measurement: at minimum temperature, relative humidity and flow at each injection and exhaust point, plus wire-surface temperature at representative locations.","Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again."],"answer":1,"explanation":"除濕系統的效果只能透過量測看見，感測器至少包括各送氣口與排氣口的溫度、相對濕度與流量，以及代表性位置的鋼絲表面溫度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The effect of a dehumidification system can only be seen through measurement: at minimum temperature, relative humidity and flow at each injection and exhaust point, plus wire-surface temperature at representative locations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b052-v13-26","title":"感測器網路與露點裕度判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Sensor network and dew-point margin: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排氣溫濕度感測器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exhaust humidity sensors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：排氣空氣 20 °C、40% RH 時露點約 6.0 °C；若夜間鋼絲 8 °C，裕度約 2.0 °C。感測器誤差 ±3% RH 時，40% 的讀值可能代表 37% 至 43%，露點約 4.9 至 7.0 °C，裕度只剩約 1.0 °C。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Exhaust air at 20 °C and 40% RH has a dew point of about 6.0 °C; with wires at 8 °C at night the margin is about 2.0 °C. With ±3% RH sensor error, a 40% reading may mean 37% to 43%, a dew point of about 4.9 to 7.0 °C, leaving a margin of only about 1.0 °C. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：安裝前逐只校正感測器並記錄序號，安裝後每年以可攜式參考儀現場比對，偏差超過允許值即更換；監控平台應同時計算露點與鋼絲溫度差，設定警報門檻，並檢查資料缺漏與時間同步。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate every sensor before installation and record serial numbers, compare annually on site with a portable reference and replace any beyond tolerance; the monitoring platform should compute dew point against wire temperature, set alarm thresholds and check for data gaps and time synchronisation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"排氣空氣 20 °C、40% RH 時露點約 6.0 °C；若夜間鋼絲 8 °C，裕度約 2.0 °C。感測器誤差 ±3% RH 時，40% 的讀值可能代表 37% 至 43%，露點約 4.9 至 7.0 °C，裕度只剩約 1.0 °C。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Exhaust air at 20 °C and 40% RH has a dew point of about 6.0 °C; with wires at 8 °C at night the margin is about 2.0 °C. With ±3% RH sensor error, a 40% reading may mean 37% to 43%, a dew point of about 4.9 to 7.0 °C, leaving a margin of only about 1.0 °C. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「感測器網路與露點裕度判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sensor network and dew-point margin\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。","只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。","排氣空氣 20 °C、40% RH 時露點約 6.0 °C；若夜間鋼絲 8 °C，裕度約 2.0 °C。"],"optionsEn":["Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money.","Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself.","Exhaust air at 20 °C and 40% RH has a dew point of about 6.0 °C; with wires at 8 °C at night the margin is about 2.0 °C."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排氣空氣 20 °C、40% RH 時露點約 6.0 °C；若夜間鋼絲 8 °C，裕度約 2.0 °C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Exhaust air at 20 °C and 40% RH has a dew point of about 6.0 °C; with wires at 8 °C at night the margin is about 2.0 °C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b052-v13-27","title":"感測器網路與露點裕度判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sensor network and dew-point margin: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排氣溫濕度感測器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exhaust humidity sensors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"安裝前逐只校正感測器並記錄序號，安裝後每年以可攜式參考儀現場比對，偏差超過允許值即更換；監控平台應同時計算露點與鋼絲溫度差，設定警報門檻，並檢查資料缺漏與時間同步。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate every sensor before installation and record serial numbers, compare annually on site with a portable reference and replace any beyond tolerance; the monitoring platform should compute dew point against wire temperature, set alarm thresholds and check for data gaps and time synchronisation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測規範應要求每個感測器的校正紀錄、年度現場比對、資料完整率門檻與「讀值長期不變」的異常偵測規則；警報要有明確的負責人與處理時限，並在每年的維護報告中彙整。","observationEn":"Site practice: The monitoring specification should require calibration records for every sensor, annual field comparison, a data-completeness threshold and a rule to detect readings that never change; alarms need a named owner and response time, summarised in the annual maintenance report.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器漂移讀值偏低時，系統看似達標而主纜實際潮濕；感測器故障輸出固定值若未被偵測，可能多年沒有人發現某區段已失去送氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sensor drifting low makes the system look on target while the cable is actually damp; a failed sensor stuck at a constant value, if undetected, can hide for years that a section has lost its supply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝前逐只校正感測器並記錄序號，安裝後每年以可攜式參考儀現場比對，偏差超過允許值即更換；監控平台應同時計算露點與鋼絲溫度差，設定警報門檻，並檢查資料缺漏與時間同步。","textEn":"Calibrate every sensor before installation and record serial numbers, compare annually on site with a portable reference and replace any beyond tolerance; the monitoring platform should compute dew point against wire temperature, set alarm thresholds and check for data gaps and time synchronisation.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測規範應要求每個感測器的校正紀錄、年度現場比對、資料完整率門檻與「讀值長期不變」的異常偵測規則；警報要有明確的負責人與處理時限，並在每年的維護報告中彙整。","textEn":"The monitoring specification should require calibration records for every sensor, annual field comparison, a data-completeness threshold and a rule to detect readings that never change; alarms need a named owner and response time, summarised in the annual maintenance report.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「感測器網路與露點裕度判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sensor network and dew-point margin\"?","options":["安裝前逐只校正感測器並記錄序號，安裝後每年以可攜式參考儀現場比對，偏差超過允許值即更換。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。"],"optionsEn":["Calibrate every sensor before installation and record serial numbers, compare annually on site with a portable reference and replace any beyond tolerance.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do."],"answer":0,"explanation":"安裝前逐只校正感測器並記錄序號，安裝後每年以可攜式參考儀現場比對，偏差超過允許值即更換；監控平台應同時計算露點與鋼絲溫度差，設定警報門檻，並檢查資料缺漏與時間同步。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate every sensor before installation and record serial numbers, compare annually on site with a portable reference and replace any beyond tolerance; the monitoring platform should compute dew point against wire temperature, set alarm thresholds and check for data gaps and time synchronisation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b052-v13-28","title":"感測器網路與露點裕度判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sensor network and dew-point margin: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排氣溫濕度感測器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exhaust humidity sensors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器漂移讀值偏低時，系統看似達標而主纜實際潮濕；感測器故障輸出固定值若未被偵測，可能多年沒有人發現某區段已失去送氣。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sensor drifting low makes the system look on target while the cable is actually damp; a failed sensor stuck at a constant value, if undetected, can hide for years that a section has lost its supply. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判讀時不應只看相對濕度，而要把空氣露點與鋼絲溫度比較：相對濕度看似達標，若夜間鋼絲溫度接近露點，仍可能結露。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Interpretation should not rest on relative humidity alone but compare air dew point with wire temperature: humidity may look on target while night-time wire temperature approaches the dew point and condensation still occurs.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器漂移讀值偏低時，系統看似達標而主纜實際潮濕；感測器故障輸出固定值若未被偵測，可能多年沒有人發現某區段已失去送氣。","textEn":"A sensor drifting low makes the system look on target while the cable is actually damp; a failed sensor stuck at a constant value, if undetected, can hide for years that a section has lost its supply.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「感測器網路與露點裕度判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sensor network and dew-point margin\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","感測器漂移讀值偏低時，系統看似達標而主纜實際潮濕；感測器故障輸出固定值若未被偵測，可能多年沒有人發現某區段已失去送氣。","裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A sensor drifting low makes the system look on target while the cable is actually damp.","Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測器漂移讀值偏低時，系統看似達標而主纜實際潮濕；感測器故障輸出固定值若未被偵測，可能多年沒有人發現某區段已失去送氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sensor drifting low makes the system look on target while the cable is actually damp; a failed sensor stuck at a constant value, if undetected, can hide for years that a section has lost its supply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b052-v13-29","title":"成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「濕潤時間與開纜比對」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time of wetness versus openings” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"除濕的目的不是讀值好看，而是讓鋼絲不再腐蝕，因此最終驗證要回到鋼絲本身。ISO 9223 以相對濕度高於 80% 且溫度高於 0 °C 的累計時數定義濕潤時間，作為大氣腐蝕性的指標之一；把纜內監測資料換算成濕潤時間，可以量化除濕前後的腐蝕環境差異。美國聯邦公路總署的入門手冊指出，膜包覆與除濕在亞洲已廣泛使用、歐洲也有應用，並建議在發現第 3 級以上腐蝕時以聲學監測偵測斷絲；監測資料與下一次開纜檢查的腐蝕分級、斷絲數比對，才能確認系統真正有效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「濕潤時間與開纜比對」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The aim of dehumidification is not good readings but wires that stop corroding, so final verification returns to the wires themselves. ISO 9223 defines time of wetness as accumulated hours with relative humidity above 80% and temperature above 0 °C, one indicator of atmospheric corrosivity; converting in-cable monitoring data into time of wetness quantifies the change in corrosive environment before and after dehumidification. The US Federal Highway Administration primer notes that membrane wrapping and dehumidification are widely used in Asia and also in Europe, and recommends acoustic monitoring for wire breaks once Stage 3 or worse corrosion is found; only comparing monitoring data with corrosion stages and broken-wire counts at the next cable opening confirms that the system works. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Time of wetness versus openings” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若除濕前纜內每年 RH > 80% 的時數為 4,000 h（約 46% 的時間），除濕後降為 80 h（約 0.9%），濕潤時間減少約 98%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If, before dehumidification, the cable spends 4,000 h a year above 80% RH (about 46% of the time) and afterwards 80 h (about 0.9%), time of wetness falls by about 98%.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「濕潤時間與開纜比對」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Time of wetness versus openings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-29-k1","title":"成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查","titleEn":"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings","text":"除濕的目的不是讀值好看，而是讓鋼絲不再腐蝕，因此最終驗證要回到鋼絲本身。ISO 9223 以相對濕度高於 80% 且溫度高於 0 °C 的累計時數定義濕潤時間，作為大氣腐蝕性的指標之一；把纜內監測資料換算成濕潤時間，可以量化除濕前後的腐蝕環境差異。","textEn":"The aim of dehumidification is not good readings but wires that stop corroding, so final verification returns to the wires themselves. ISO 9223 defines time of wetness as accumulated hours with relative humidity above 80% and temperature above 0 °C, one indicator of atmospheric corrosivity; converting in-cable monitoring data into time of wetness quantifies the change in corrosive environment before and after dehumidification.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings\" is correct?","options":["裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。","除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。","除濕的目的不是讀值好看，而是讓鋼絲不再腐蝕，因此最終驗證要回到鋼絲本身。"],"optionsEn":["Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again.","Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.","The aim of dehumidification is not good readings but wires that stop corroding, so final verification returns to the wires themselves."],"answer":2,"explanation":"除濕的目的不是讀值好看，而是讓鋼絲不再腐蝕，因此最終驗證要回到鋼絲本身。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The aim of dehumidification is not good readings but wires that stop corroding, so final verification returns to the wires themselves. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b052-v13-30","title":"成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濕潤時間與開纜比對」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time of wetness versus openings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若除濕前纜內每年 RH > 80% 的時數為 4,000 h（約 46% 的時間），除濕後降為 80 h（約 0.9%），濕潤時間減少約 98%。若腐蝕速率約與濕潤時間成正比，鋅層消耗年數由 10 年級延長到數百年級。比例關係為教學簡化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If, before dehumidification, the cable spends 4,000 h a year above 80% RH (about 46% of the time) and afterwards 80 h (about 0.9%), time of wetness falls by about 98%. If corrosion rate scales roughly with time of wetness, zinc life stretches from the order of ten years to the order of centuries. The proportionality is a teaching simplification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把每個區段的監測資料逐年換算成濕潤時數與露點裕度，選擇改造前曾有腐蝕的位置在數年後開窗，以相同的楔線與分級方法記錄，與改造前結果並列比較；聲學監測事件則對照開窗位置確認是否為斷絲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert each section's monitoring data into annual wet hours and dew-point margin, reopen windows some years later at locations that showed corrosion before the retrofit, recording with the same wedge lines and staging method for side-by-side comparison; check acoustic events against opening locations to confirm whether they were wire breaks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若除濕前纜內每年 RH > 80% 的時數為 4,000 h（約 46% 的時間），除濕後降為 80 h（約 0.9%），濕潤時間減少約 98%。若腐蝕速率約與濕潤時間成正比，鋅層消耗年數由 10 年級延長到數百年級。比例關係為教學簡化。","textEn":"If, before dehumidification, the cable spends 4,000 h a year above 80% RH (about 46% of the time) and afterwards 80 h (about 0.9%), time of wetness falls by about 98%. If corrosion rate scales roughly with time of wetness, zinc life stretches from the order of ten years to the order of centuries. The proportionality is a teaching simplification.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings\", which statement holds?","options":["若除濕前纜內每年 RH > 80% 的時數為 4,000 h（約 46% 的時間），除濕後降為 80 h（約 0.9%），濕潤時間減少約 98%。","主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。","包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。"],"optionsEn":["If, before dehumidification, the cable spends 4,000 h a year above 80% RH (about 46% of the time) and afterwards 80 h (about 0.9%), time of wetness falls by about 98%.","With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside.","The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若除濕前纜內每年 RH > 80% 的時數為 4,000 h（約 46% 的時間），除濕後降為 80 h（約 0.9%），濕潤時間減少約 98%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If, before dehumidification, the cable spends 4,000 h a year above 80% RH (about 46% of the time) and afterwards 80 h (about 0.9%), time of wetness falls by about 98%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b052-v13-31","title":"成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濕潤時間與開纜比對」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time of wetness versus openings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把每個區段的監測資料逐年換算成濕潤時數與露點裕度，選擇改造前曾有腐蝕的位置在數年後開窗，以相同的楔線與分級方法記錄，與改造前結果並列比較；聲學監測事件則對照開窗位置確認是否為斷絲。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert each section's monitoring data into annual wet hours and dew-point margin, reopen windows some years later at locations that showed corrosion before the retrofit, recording with the same wedge lines and staging method for side-by-side comparison; check acoustic events against opening locations to confirm whether they were wire breaks. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主應把除濕系統的監測資料、聲學監測與開纜檢查整合成同一套主纜狀態評估，訂出改造後的首次複查時程（例如數年內一次），並在評估報告中分開記載改造前的既有損傷與改造後的新增變化。","observationEn":"Site practice: The owner should combine dehumidification monitoring, acoustic monitoring and cable openings into one cable-condition assessment, set the first post-retrofit re-inspection (for example within a few years), and record existing pre-retrofit damage separately from new changes in the assessment report.","failure":"注意干擾：只以排氣濕度證明成效而從未開纜比對，可能長期誤判；已經產生裂紋的鋼絲即使在乾燥環境中也不會恢復強度，若未把改造前的劣化納入評估，可能高估剩餘安全係數。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Proving effectiveness only by exhaust humidity, never by reopening the cable, can mislead for years; wires already cracked do not regain strength in dry air, so ignoring pre-retrofit damage can overstate the remaining safety factor. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把每個區段的監測資料逐年換算成濕潤時數與露點裕度，選擇改造前曾有腐蝕的位置在數年後開窗，以相同的楔線與分級方法記錄，與改造前結果並列比較；聲學監測事件則對照開窗位置確認是否為斷絲。","textEn":"Convert each section's monitoring data into annual wet hours and dew-point margin, reopen windows some years later at locations that showed corrosion before the retrofit, recording with the same wedge lines and staging method for side-by-side comparison; check acoustic events against opening locations to confirm whether they were wire breaks.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主應把除濕系統的監測資料、聲學監測與開纜檢查整合成同一套主纜狀態評估，訂出改造後的首次複查時程（例如數年內一次），並在評估報告中分開記載改造前的既有損傷與改造後的新增變化。","textEn":"The owner should combine dehumidification monitoring, acoustic monitoring and cable openings into one cable-condition assessment, set the first post-retrofit re-inspection (for example within a few years), and record existing pre-retrofit damage separately from new changes in the assessment report.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把每個區段的監測資料逐年換算成濕潤時數與露點裕度，選擇改造前曾有腐蝕的位置在數年後開窗，以相同的楔線與分級方法記錄，與改造前結果並列比較。","除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Convert each section's monitoring data into annual wet hours and dew-point margin, reopen windows some years later at locations that showed corrosion before the retrofit, recording with the same wedge lines and staging method for side-by-side comparison.","A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把每個區段的監測資料逐年換算成濕潤時數與露點裕度，選擇改造前曾有腐蝕的位置在數年後開窗，以相同的楔線與分級方法記錄，與改造前結果並列比較；聲學監測事件則對照開窗位置確認是否為斷絲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert each section's monitoring data into annual wet hours and dew-point margin, reopen windows some years later at locations that showed corrosion before the retrofit, recording with the same wedge lines and staging method for side-by-side comparison; check acoustic events against opening locations to confirm whether they were wire breaks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b052-v13-32","title":"成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濕潤時間與開纜比對」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time of wetness versus openings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以排氣濕度證明成效而從未開纜比對，可能長期誤判；已經產生裂紋的鋼絲即使在乾燥環境中也不會恢復強度，若未把改造前的劣化納入評估，可能高估剩餘安全係數。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Proving effectiveness only by exhaust humidity, never by reopening the cable, can mislead for years; wires already cracked do not regain strength in dry air, so ignoring pre-retrofit damage can overstate the remaining safety factor. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：美國聯邦公路總署的入門手冊指出，膜包覆與除濕在亞洲已廣泛使用、歐洲也有應用，並建議在發現第 3 級以上腐蝕時以聲學監測偵測斷絲；監測資料與下一次開纜檢查的腐蝕分級、斷絲數比對，才能確認系統真正有效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The US Federal Highway Administration primer notes that membrane wrapping and dehumidification are widely used in Asia and also in Europe, and recommends acoustic monitoring for wire breaks once Stage 3 or worse corrosion is found; only comparing monitoring data with corrosion stages and broken-wire counts at the next cable opening confirms that the system works.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝了除濕系統之後，主纜就不需要再開纜檢查。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a dehumidification system is installed, the cable never needs opening again.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以排氣濕度證明成效而從未開纜比對，可能長期誤判；已經產生裂紋的鋼絲即使在乾燥環境中也不會恢復強度，若未把改造前的劣化納入評估，可能高估剩餘安全係數。","textEn":"Proving effectiveness only by exhaust humidity, never by reopening the cable, can mislead for years; wires already cracked do not regain strength in dry air, so ignoring pre-retrofit damage can overstate the remaining safety factor.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「成效驗證：濕潤時間與開纜檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Verifying effectiveness: time of wetness and cable openings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。","只以排氣濕度證明成效而從未開纜比對，可能長期誤判；已經產生裂紋的鋼絲即使在乾燥環境中也不會恢復強度，若未把改造前的劣化納入評估，可能高估剩餘安全係數。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.","Proving effectiveness only by exhaust humidity, never by reopening the cable, can mislead for years."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只以排氣濕度證明成效而從未開纜比對，可能長期誤判；已經產生裂紋的鋼絲即使在乾燥環境中也不會恢復強度，若未把改造前的劣化納入評估，可能高估剩餘安全係數。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Proving effectiveness only by exhaust humidity, never by reopening the cable, can mislead for years; wires already cracked do not regain strength in dry air, so ignoring pre-retrofit damage can overstate the remaining safety factor. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b052-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「運轉能耗與設備維護」與「除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Running energy and plant maintenance\" and \"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b052-v13-33","title":"運轉能耗與設備維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Running energy and plant maintenance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「風機與再生能耗」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fan and regeneration energy” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"除濕系統需要數十年連續運轉，能耗與設備維護是營運成本的主要部分。能耗來自兩處：推動空氣通過管路與主纜空隙的風機，以及加熱再生空氣使吸附轉輪恢復吸濕能力的加熱器，後者通常較大。維護項目包括過濾器更換、轉輪與密封檢查、風機軸承、預冷盤管清潔與凝結水排放、控制系統與感測器校正。本州四國連絡橋的經驗也顯示，系統需要依實際運轉持續改善，例如針對夏季高濕加裝預冷設備。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「風機與再生能耗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dehumidification system runs continuously for decades, so energy and plant maintenance dominate operating cost. Energy goes in two places: fans that push air through ducts and cable voids, and heaters that warm regeneration air to restore the desiccant rotor, the latter usually being larger. Maintenance covers filter changes, rotor and seal checks, fan bearings, pre-cooler coil cleaning and condensate drainage, and control-system and sensor calibration. The Honshu-Shikoku experience also shows that a system needs continuous improvement from operating data, such as adding pre-coolers for humid summers. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fan and regeneration energy” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：風機功率 P = Q·Δp/η。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Fan power P = Q·Δp/η.","failure":"常見誤解：「除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「風機與再生能耗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fan and regeneration energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-33-k1","title":"運轉能耗與設備維護","titleEn":"Running energy and plant maintenance","text":"除濕系統需要數十年連續運轉，能耗與設備維護是營運成本的主要部分。能耗來自兩處：推動空氣通過管路與主纜空隙的風機，以及加熱再生空氣使吸附轉輪恢復吸濕能力的加熱器，後者通常較大。","textEn":"A dehumidification system runs continuously for decades, so energy and plant maintenance dominate operating cost. Energy goes in two places: fans that push air through ducts and cable voids, and heaters that warm regeneration air to restore the desiccant rotor, the latter usually being larger.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「運轉能耗與設備維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Running energy and plant maintenance\" is correct?","options":["除濕系統需要數十年連續運轉，能耗與設備維護是營運成本的主要部分。","除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。","主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。"],"optionsEn":["A dehumidification system runs continuously for decades, so energy and plant maintenance dominate operating cost.","Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.","Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money."],"answer":0,"explanation":"除濕系統需要數十年連續運轉，能耗與設備維護是營運成本的主要部分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dehumidification system runs continuously for decades, so energy and plant maintenance dominate operating cost. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b052-v13-34","title":"運轉能耗與設備維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Running energy and plant maintenance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風機與再生能耗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fan and regeneration energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：風機功率 P = Q·Δp/η。取 Q = 0.2 m³/s、Δp = 3,000 Pa、效率 η = 0.5：P = 0.2×3,000/0.5 = 1,200 W。再生加熱器 10 kW、平均負載率 50%，年耗電約 10×8,760×0.5 = 43,800 kWh，遠大於風機的約 10,500 kWh。若預冷降低吸附負荷四成，再生能耗可望同步下降。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Fan power P = Q·Δp/η. With Q = 0.2 m³/s, Δp = 3,000 Pa and efficiency η = 0.5: P = 0.2×3,000/0.5 = 1,200 W. A 10 kW regeneration heater at 50% average duty uses about 10×8,760×0.5 = 43,800 kWh a year, far more than the fan's roughly 10,500 kWh. If pre-cooling cuts the desiccant load by 40%, regeneration energy can fall in step. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以電錶分別記錄風機、再生加熱與預冷的耗電，與除濕量、外氣條件一起分析每公斤除濕量的能耗趨勢；能耗上升而除濕量不變時，檢查過濾器堵塞、轉輪劣化或洩漏增加。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Meter fan, regeneration and pre-cooler consumption separately and analyse energy per kilogram of moisture removed against outdoor conditions; when energy rises for the same moisture removal, check for clogged filters, rotor deterioration or increased leakage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"風機功率 P = Q·Δp/η。取 Q = 0.2 m³/s、Δp = 3,000 Pa、效率 η = 0.5：P = 0.2×3,000/0.5 = 1,200 W。再生加熱器 10 kW、平均負載率 50%，年耗電約 10×8,760×0.5 = 43,800 kWh，遠大於風機的約 10,500 kWh。若預冷降低吸附負荷四成，再生能耗可望同步下降。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Fan power P = Q·Δp/η. With Q = 0.2 m³/s, Δp = 3,000 Pa and efficiency η = 0.5: P = 0.2×3,000/0.5 = 1,200 W. A 10 kW regeneration heater at 50% average duty uses about 10×8,760×0.5 = 43,800 kWh a year, far more than the fan's roughly 10,500 kWh. If pre-cooling cuts the desiccant load by 40%, regeneration energy can fall in step. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「運轉能耗與設備維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Running energy and plant maintenance\", which statement holds?","options":["只要把除濕機開大，乾燥空氣就能自然流遍整條主纜。","風機功率 P = Q·Δp/η。","除濕機只要選一台夠大的家用或倉庫型機器即可。"],"optionsEn":["Just turn the dehumidifier up and dry air will spread along the whole cable by itself.","Fan power P = Q·Δp/η.","Any large household or warehouse dehumidifier will do."],"answer":1,"explanation":"風機功率 P = Q·Δp/η。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Fan power P = Q·Δp/η. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b052-v13-35","title":"運轉能耗與設備維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Running energy and plant maintenance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風機與再生能耗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fan and regeneration energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以電錶分別記錄風機、再生加熱與預冷的耗電，與除濕量、外氣條件一起分析每公斤除濕量的能耗趨勢；能耗上升而除濕量不變時，檢查過濾器堵塞、轉輪劣化或洩漏增加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Meter fan, regeneration and pre-cooler consumption separately and analyse energy per kilogram of moisture removed against outdoor conditions; when energy rises for the same moisture removal, check for clogged filters, rotor deterioration or increased leakage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：維護手冊應列出各設備的檢查週期、更換零件清單、能耗基準與性能退化判斷準則，並把能耗與除濕量的比值作為年度報告的關鍵指標；任何節能措施都必須先評估對纜內濕度的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: The maintenance manual should list inspection intervals, spare parts, energy baselines and degradation criteria for every item of plant, with energy per unit of moisture removed as a key annual indicator; any energy-saving measure must first be assessed for its effect on cable humidity.","failure":"注意干擾：為節省能源而降低送氣量或關閉部分機組，排氣濕度在數週內回升；過濾器長期未更換使壓降增加、流量下降，而控制系統若只看風機運轉狀態，可能不會發出警報。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cutting supply flow or switching off units to save energy lets exhaust humidity climb within weeks; filters left unchanged raise pressure drop and cut flow, and a control system that watches only whether fans are running may never alarm. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以電錶分別記錄風機、再生加熱與預冷的耗電，與除濕量、外氣條件一起分析每公斤除濕量的能耗趨勢；能耗上升而除濕量不變時，檢查過濾器堵塞、轉輪劣化或洩漏增加。","textEn":"Meter fan, regeneration and pre-cooler consumption separately and analyse energy per kilogram of moisture removed against outdoor conditions; when energy rises for the same moisture removal, check for clogged filters, rotor deterioration or increased leakage.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"維護手冊應列出各設備的檢查週期、更換零件清單、能耗基準與性能退化判斷準則，並把能耗與除濕量的比值作為年度報告的關鍵指標；任何節能措施都必須先評估對纜內濕度的影響。","textEn":"The maintenance manual should list inspection intervals, spare parts, energy baselines and degradation criteria for every item of plant, with energy per unit of moisture removed as a key annual indicator; any energy-saving measure must first be assessed for its effect on cable humidity.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「運轉能耗與設備維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Running energy and plant maintenance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","除濕系統一啟動，主纜內部在幾天內就會變乾。","以電錶分別記錄風機、再生加熱與預冷的耗電，與除濕量、外氣條件一起分析每公斤除濕量的能耗趨勢；能耗上升而除濕量不變時，檢查過濾器堵塞、轉輪劣化或洩漏增加。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once switched on, a dehumidification system dries the cable within a few days.","Meter fan, regeneration and pre-cooler consumption separately and analyse energy per kilogram of moisture removed against outdoor conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以電錶分別記錄風機、再生加熱與預冷的耗電，與除濕量、外氣條件一起分析每公斤除濕量的能耗趨勢；能耗上升而除濕量不變時，檢查過濾器堵塞、轉輪劣化或洩漏增加。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Meter fan, regeneration and pre-cooler consumption separately and analyse energy per kilogram of moisture removed against outdoor conditions; when energy rises for the same moisture removal, check for clogged filters, rotor deterioration or increased leakage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b052-v13-36","title":"運轉能耗與設備維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Running energy and plant maintenance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風機與再生能耗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fan and regeneration energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為節省能源而降低送氣量或關閉部分機組，排氣濕度在數週內回升；過濾器長期未更換使壓降增加、流量下降，而控制系統若只看風機運轉狀態，可能不會發出警報。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cutting supply flow or switching off units to save energy lets exhaust humidity climb within weeks; filters left unchanged raise pressure drop and cut flow, and a control system that watches only whether fans are running may never alarm. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本州四國連絡橋的經驗也顯示，系統需要依實際運轉持續改善，例如針對夏季高濕加裝預冷設備。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Honshu-Shikoku experience also shows that a system needs continuous improvement from operating data, such as adding pre-coolers for humid summers.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「除濕系統安裝後幾乎不耗能，也不需要例行維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once installed, a dehumidification system uses almost no energy and needs no routine maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為節省能源而降低送氣量或關閉部分機組，排氣濕度在數週內回升；過濾器長期未更換使壓降增加、流量下降，而控制系統若只看風機運轉狀態，可能不會發出警報。","textEn":"Cutting supply flow or switching off units to save energy lets exhaust humidity climb within weeks; filters left unchanged raise pressure drop and cut flow, and a control system that watches only whether fans are running may never alarm.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「運轉能耗與設備維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Running energy and plant maintenance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["為節省能源而降低送氣量或關閉部分機組，排氣濕度在數週內回升；過濾器長期未更換使壓降增加、流量下降，而控制系統若只看風機運轉狀態，可能不會發出警報。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。"],"optionsEn":["Cutting supply flow or switching off units to save energy lets exhaust humidity climb within weeks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money."],"answer":0,"explanation":"為節省能源而降低送氣量或關閉部分機組，排氣濕度在數週內回升；過濾器長期未更換使壓降增加、流量下降，而控制系統若只看風機運轉狀態，可能不會發出警報。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cutting supply flow or switching off units to save energy lets exhaust humidity climb within weeks; filters left unchanged raise pressure drop and cut flow, and a control system that watches only whether fans are running may never alarm. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b052-v13-37","title":"除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「除濕與重塗的生命週期」如何影響懸索橋主纜除濕系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-cable dehumidification systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公開資料指出，大貝爾特東橋通車約 15 年時主纜尚未發現鏽蝕，原本規劃的是重新塗裝，業主最後選擇投入更高的初始費用安裝密封除濕系統。這個決策的關鍵在於：重新塗裝只能維持外層，無法處理已進入主纜內部或日後滲入的水分；而主纜一旦因腐蝕需要補強或限載，代價遠高於任何防蝕措施。本州四國連絡橋以 200 年以上的使用為目標、以預防保全降低生命週期成本，也是同一邏輯。決策時必須把不確定的未來劣化風險放進比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「除濕與重塗的生命週期」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Public accounts note that after about 15 years in service no rust had been found in the Great Belt East Bridge cables; repainting had been planned, but the owner chose a higher initial outlay on a sealed dehumidification system. The key is that repainting only maintains the outer skin and does nothing about water already inside the cable or entering later, while a cable that needs strengthening or load limits because of corrosion costs far more than any protection. The Honshu-Shikoku bridges' target of 200 years or more, with preventive maintenance to minimise life-cycle cost, follows the same logic. The decision must bring the uncertain risk of future deterioration into the comparison. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以相對成本單位、折現率 3%、100 年比較。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Compare in relative cost units at 3% discount over 100 years.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「除濕與重塗的生命週期」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-37-k1","title":"除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策","titleEn":"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting","text":"公開資料指出，大貝爾特東橋通車約 15 年時主纜尚未發現鏽蝕，原本規劃的是重新塗裝，業主最後選擇投入更高的初始費用安裝密封除濕系統。這個決策的關鍵在於：重新塗裝只能維持外層，無法處理已進入主纜內部或日後滲入的水分；而主纜一旦因腐蝕需要補強或限載，代價遠高於任何防蝕措施。","textEn":"Public accounts note that after about 15 years in service no rust had been found in the Great Belt East Bridge cables; repainting had been planned, but the owner chose a higher initial outlay on a sealed dehumidification system. The key is that repainting only maintains the outer skin and does nothing about water already inside the cable or entering later, while a cable that needs strengthening or load limits because of corrosion costs far more than any protection.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting\" is correct?","options":["主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。","公開資料指出，大貝爾特東橋通車約 15 年時主纜尚未發現鏽蝕，原本規劃的是重新塗裝，業主最後選擇投入更高的初始費用安裝密封除濕系統。","主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。"],"optionsEn":["Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money.","Public accounts note that after about 15 years in service no rust had been found in the Great Belt East Bridge cables.","With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開資料指出，大貝爾特東橋通車約 15 年時主纜尚未發現鏽蝕，原本規劃的是重新塗裝，業主最後選擇投入更高的初始費用安裝密封除濕系統。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Public accounts note that after about 15 years in service no rust had been found in the Great Belt East Bridge cables; repainting had been planned, but the owner chose a higher initial outlay on a sealed dehumidification system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b052-v13-38","title":"除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策：定量估算","titleEn":"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「除濕與重塗的生命週期」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以相對成本單位、折現率 3%、100 年比較。重塗每 15 年 1.0 單位：現值 ≈ 1 + 0.642 + 0.412 + 0.264 + 0.170 + 0.109 + 0.070 ≈ 2.67。除濕初設 4.7、年運轉 0.05（年金係數 31.6）、每 25 年更換設備 0.8：現值 ≈ 4.7 + 1.58 + 0.65 ≈ 6.93。差額 4.26 單位，若重塗方案在第 50 年有 50% 機率需要 37 單位的主纜介入，其期望現值 0.5×37×0.228 ≈ 4.22，兩者接近打平。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Compare in relative cost units at 3% discount over 100 years. Repainting at 1.0 unit every 15 years has a present value ≈ 1 + 0.642 + 0.412 + 0.264 + 0.170 + 0.109 + 0.070 ≈ 2.67. Dehumidification at 4.7 initial, 0.05 a year (annuity factor 31.6) and 0.8 for plant renewal every 25 years has ≈ 4.7 + 1.58 + 0.65 ≈ 6.93. The difference is 4.26 units; if the repainting option carries a 50% chance of a 37-unit cable intervention at year 50, its expected present value 0.5×37×0.228 ≈ 4.22 nearly closes the gap. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：決策文件應列出現況檢查與開纜結果、各方案的成本與時程假設、劣化與介入機率的依據，並做折現率、劣化速率與介入成本的敏感度分析；由業主的技術委員會審查，並在改造後依實測資料檢討假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The decision file should set out current inspection and opening results, cost and timing assumptions for each option, the basis for deterioration and intervention probabilities, and sensitivity analyses on discount rate, deterioration rate and intervention cost; the owner's technical committee reviews it, and assumptions are revisited with measured data after the retrofit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以相對成本單位、折現率 3%、100 年比較。重塗每 15 年 1.0 單位：現值 ≈ 1 + 0.642 + 0.412 + 0.264 + 0.170 + 0.109 + 0.070 ≈ 2.67。除濕初設 4.7、年運轉 0.05（年金係數 31.6）、每 25 年更換設備 0.8：現值 ≈ 4.7 + 1.58 + 0.65 ≈ 6.93。差額 4.26 單位，若重塗方案在第 50 年有 50% 機率需要 37 單位的主纜介入，其期望現值 0.5×37×0.228 ≈ 4.22，兩者接近打平。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Compare in relative cost units at 3% discount over 100 years. Repainting at 1.0 unit every 15 years has a present value ≈ 1 + 0.642 + 0.412 + 0.264 + 0.170 + 0.109 + 0.070 ≈ 2.67. Dehumidification at 4.7 initial, 0.05 a year (annuity factor 31.6) and 0.8 for plant renewal every 25 years has ≈ 4.7 + 1.58 + 0.65 ≈ 6.93. The difference is 4.26 units; if the repainting option carries a 50% chance of a 37-unit cable intervention at year 50, its expected present value 0.5×37×0.228 ≈ 4.22 nearly closes the gap. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting\", which statement holds?","options":["包覆材料越厚越好，索夾處的細部影響不大。","除濕改造只是加一層外皮，可以在任何天氣快速完成。","以相對成本單位、折現率 3%、100 年比較。"],"optionsEn":["The thicker the wrap the better; details at cable bands hardly matter.","A dehumidification retrofit just adds a skin and can be done quickly in any weather.","Compare in relative cost units at 3% discount over 100 years."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以相對成本單位、折現率 3%、100 年比較。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Compare in relative cost units at 3% discount over 100 years. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b052-v13-39","title":"除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「除濕與重塗的生命週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"決策文件應列出現況檢查與開纜結果、各方案的成本與時程假設、劣化與介入機率的依據，並做折現率、劣化速率與介入成本的敏感度分析；由業主的技術委員會審查，並在改造後依實測資料檢討假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The decision file should set out current inspection and opening results, cost and timing assumptions for each option, the basis for deterioration and intervention probabilities, and sensitivity analyses on discount rate, deterioration rate and intervention cost; the owner's technical committee reviews it, and assumptions are revisited with measured data after the retrofit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主應在資產管理計畫中明列主纜防蝕策略的決策準則、檢討週期與觸發條件，並把除濕系統的設計、調試、監測與維護資料作為完整的交接包，確保日後的管理者能延續同一套證據鏈。","observationEn":"Site practice: The owner's asset-management plan should state the decision criteria, review cycle and triggers for cable corrosion strategy, and hand over the dehumidification design, commissioning, monitoring and maintenance records as one package so future managers inherit the same chain of evidence.","failure":"注意干擾：只比較直接工程費而不考慮主纜劣化風險，會系統性地偏向延後投資；等到開纜發現大量第 4 級腐蝕或斷絲才改造，除濕雖可阻止惡化，卻無法恢復已損失的強度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing only direct works cost without cable-deterioration risk systematically favours delay; retrofitting only after openings reveal widespread Stage 4 corrosion or broken wires stops further damage but cannot restore the strength already lost. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"決策文件應列出現況檢查與開纜結果、各方案的成本與時程假設、劣化與介入機率的依據，並做折現率、劣化速率與介入成本的敏感度分析；由業主的技術委員會審查，並在改造後依實測資料檢討假設。","textEn":"The decision file should set out current inspection and opening results, cost and timing assumptions for each option, the basis for deterioration and intervention probabilities, and sensitivity analyses on discount rate, deterioration rate and intervention cost; the owner's technical committee reviews it, and assumptions are revisited with measured data after the retrofit.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主應在資產管理計畫中明列主纜防蝕策略的決策準則、檢討週期與觸發條件，並把除濕系統的設計、調試、監測與維護資料作為完整的交接包，確保日後的管理者能延續同一套證據鏈。","textEn":"The owner's asset-management plan should state the decision criteria, review cycle and triggers for cable corrosion strategy, and hand over the dehumidification design, commissioning, monitoring and maintenance records as one package so future managers inherit the same chain of evidence.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting\"?","options":["決策文件應列出現況檢查與開纜結果、各方案的成本與時程假設、劣化與介入機率的依據，並做折現率、劣化速率與介入成本的敏感度分析。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要相對濕度低於目標，主纜就不可能結露。"],"optionsEn":["The decision file should set out current inspection and opening results, cost and timing assumptions for each option, the basis for deterioration and intervention probabilities, and sensitivity analyses on discount rate, deterioration rate and intervention cost.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If relative humidity is below target, the cable cannot have condensation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"決策文件應列出現況檢查與開纜結果、各方案的成本與時程假設、劣化與介入機率的依據，並做折現率、劣化速率與介入成本的敏感度分析；由業主的技術委員會審查，並在改造後依實測資料檢討假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The decision file should set out current inspection and opening results, cost and timing assumptions for each option, the basis for deterioration and intervention probabilities, and sensitivity analyses on discount rate, deterioration rate and intervention cost; the owner's technical committee reviews it, and assumptions are revisited with measured data after the retrofit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b052-v13-40","title":"除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策：失效診斷","titleEn":"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b052-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「除濕與重塗的生命週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dehumidify-or-repaint life cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只比較直接工程費而不考慮主纜劣化風險，會系統性地偏向延後投資；等到開纜發現大量第 4 級腐蝕或斷絲才改造，除濕雖可阻止惡化，卻無法恢復已損失的強度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing only direct works cost without cable-deterioration risk systematically favours delay; retrofitting only after openings reveal widespread Stage 4 corrosion or broken wires stops further damage but cannot restore the strength already lost. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：決策時必須把不確定的未來劣化風險放進比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The decision must bring the uncertain risk of future deterioration into the comparison.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜還沒生鏽就安裝除濕系統，是浪費預算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing dehumidification before a cable shows rust is a waste of money.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b052-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只比較直接工程費而不考慮主纜劣化風險，會系統性地偏向延後投資；等到開纜發現大量第 4 級腐蝕或斷絲才改造，除濕雖可阻止惡化，卻無法恢復已損失的強度。","textEn":"Comparing only direct works cost without cable-deterioration risk systematically favours delay; retrofitting only after openings reveal widespread Stage 4 corrosion or broken wires stops further damage but cannot restore the strength already lost.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]},{"id":"b052-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「除濕與重新塗裝的生命週期決策」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Life-cycle decision: dehumidification versus repainting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只比較直接工程費而不考慮主纜劣化風險，會系統性地偏向延後投資；等到開纜發現大量第 4 級腐蝕或斷絲才改造，除濕雖可阻止惡化，卻無法恢復已損失的強度。","主纜外層有纏絲與塗裝，只要外觀完好，內部就一定乾燥。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Comparing only direct works cost without cable-deterioration risk systematically favours delay.","With wrapping and paint outside, an intact-looking cable must be dry inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只比較直接工程費而不考慮主纜劣化風險，會系統性地偏向延後投資；等到開纜發現大量第 4 級腐蝕或斷絲才改造，除濕雖可阻止惡化，卻無法恢復已損失的強度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing only direct works cost without cable-deterioration risk systematically favours delay; retrofitting only after openings reveal widespread Stage 4 corrosion or broken wires stops further damage but cannot restore the strength already lost. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-policy","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt","v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v13s-wiki-great-belt-bridge"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
